<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/1483695f-bbd2-49c5-ae63-7f3ec896157d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Alternative rejected in commit cd5cee9a68: enabling cls-thing, cls-nothing1, and prp-ap by default (rather than gating behind an opt-in --complete flag) was considered and rejected because, per the README, these rules \"are spec-correct but produce triples with zero practical inference value\" -- gating them avoids bloating every default reasoning run while still allowing conformance testing against reference reasoners like owlrl via --complete." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
