<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/408e1ee3-f208-458d-bc46-c7a0c3be13e2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Pass delta-add's Delta as (Ptr Delta) to mutate in place: rejected because every caller threads the returned Delta via set!, so a local mut copy keeps the existing functional-update contract with no call-site churn." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/4f7cfb81-f4f2-462b-bfa7-c1c4f59b9f94> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Alternative> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/4f7cfb81-f4f2-462b-bfa7-c1c4f59b9f94> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Keep seeding the initial Delta via indexed-graph-for-each + delta-add per triple, which (as a side effect) populates Delta's seen hash set for dedup — the prior implementation, and the pattern the earlier \"Stream graph matches via indexed-graph-for-each\" decision established for this exact call site. Rejected because the initial delta is read-only and graph triples are already deduplicated, so the seen-set population was pure overhead: the new code comment measures this at ~1.85 GB for a 7.7M-triple graph." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/4f7cfb81-f4f2-462b-bfa7-c1c4f59b9f94> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
