<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/05b05f38-0af8-4e10-a92f-87f1ce1e23ea> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/05b05f38-0af8-4e10-a92f-87f1ce1e23ea> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "CLI --quiet emits one-line benchmark-parseable summary" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/05b05f38-0af8-4e10-a92f-87f1ce1e23ea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/e71422b6-0c80-4741-aa68-a27243061168> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/05b05f38-0af8-4e10-a92f-87f1ce1e23ea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/05b05f38-0af8-4e10-a92f-87f1ce1e23ea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "cli/main.slop's `--quiet` mode is no longer fully silent on success or inconsistency: a new block, commented \"Always print machine-parseable summary,\" now runs `(when quiet ...)` in both the reason-success and reason-inconsistent branches, printing a single line of the form `<input-path>: <parse-elapsed> parse, <reason-elapsed> reason, <input-size> -> <triple-count> triples` (with a trailing `[INCONSISTENT]` marker in the failure case), alongside the pre-existing `(when (not quiet) ...)` multi-line human-readable report. Evidence: commit 10f2845884 diff on cli/main.slop, both new `(when quiet (print input-path) ... (println \" triples\"))` blocks, added in the same commit as the new cli/tests/benchmark.sh script, which runs `$GROWL --quiet \"$f\"` three times over each of several ontology fixtures (bfo-core, pizza, CommonCoreOntologiesMerged, Brick, schemaorg) to collect timing." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/05b05f38-0af8-4e10-a92f-87f1ce1e23ea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/05b05f38-0af8-4e10-a92f-87f1ce1e23ea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-07T04:53:15Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/05b05f38-0af8-4e10-a92f-87f1ce1e23ea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "CLI --quiet emits one-line benchmark-parseable summary" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/05b05f38-0af8-4e10-a92f-87f1ce1e23ea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8594f3ad-fe7b-443a-b183-1e0b2dcc5a03> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/07a4aa19-53ff-4ac9-86f2-1cb9fbb3f597> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/07a4aa19-53ff-4ac9-86f2-1cb9fbb3f597> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Uncapped arena by default for CLI builds" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/07a4aa19-53ff-4ac9-86f2-1cb9fbb3f597> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/74af8f69-d68a-4db6-a495-07bb196e4866> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/07a4aa19-53ff-4ac9-86f2-1cb9fbb3f597> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/07a4aa19-53ff-4ac9-86f2-1cb9fbb3f597> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Growl's default C build (Makefile `cli`/`release` targets) and the CLI/CLI-test SLOP build configs (cli/slop.toml, cli/tests/slop.toml) now compile unconditionally with -DSLOP_ARENA_NO_CAP / `no_arena_cap = true`, removing the prior configurable `ARENA` byte-ceiling (default 8589934592 / 8GB via `-DSLOP_ARENA_MAX_TOTAL_BYTES=$(ARENA)UL`) entirely, rather than raising the default cap or leaving the cap opt-out.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit d26d5120 (merge PR #3 \"Completing\") diff on Makefile — drops the `ARENA ?= 8589934592` variable, and both the default CFLAGS and the `release:` target's CFLAGS replace `-DSLOP_ARENA_MAX_TOTAL_BYTES=$(ARENA)UL` with `-DSLOP_ARENA_NO_CAP`. cli/slop.toml's `[build]` section replaces `arena_cap = 8589934592  # 8GB cap` with `no_arena_cap = true`; cli/tests/slop.toml's `[build]` section likewise replaces `arena_cap = 8589934592  # 8GB` with `no_arena_cap = true`. This activates, as the new default across all CLI/test/release build targets, the SLOP_ARENA_NO_CAP escape hatch that an earlier commit added as dormant, unused infrastructure (see \"SLOP_ARENA_NO_CAP build-time arena-cap bypass\")." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/07a4aa19-53ff-4ac9-86f2-1cb9fbb3f597> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/07a4aa19-53ff-4ac9-86f2-1cb9fbb3f597> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-08T00:55:37Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/07a4aa19-53ff-4ac9-86f2-1cb9fbb3f597> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Uncapped arena by default for CLI builds" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/07a4aa19-53ff-4ac9-86f2-1cb9fbb3f597> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/76504eee-4561-4806-8601-5690ce5d0e45> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/07a4aa19-53ff-4ac9-86f2-1cb9fbb3f597> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/ef0a4608-7fd7-45ec-b379-c77048935c13> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0950df26-7f03-4085-84fb-523dc9b7145a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0950df26-7f03-4085-84fb-523dc9b7145a> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Consume shared C modules via slop-std-sys/slop-rdf-sys" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0950df26-7f03-4085-84fb-523dc9b7145a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/74af8f69-d68a-4db6-a495-07bb196e4866> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0950df26-7f03-4085-84fb-523dc9b7145a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/833a482a-9217-4511-99e7-1166a8c28fbb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0950df26-7f03-4085-84fb-523dc9b7145a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0950df26-7f03-4085-84fb-523dc9b7145a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Growl's Rust crate now vendors and compiles only its own C modules (cax, cls, dt, engine, eq, filter, growl, prp, scm, types) itself; the shared modules previously copied wholesale into rust/csrc/ are instead consumed as native static libraries bundled inside the slop-std-sys and slop-rdf-sys crates (git = slop-lang/slop-sys, tag v0.2.1).\n\nWhy + evidence: commit c9a80f902b — rust/Cargo.toml adds `[dependencies] slop-std-sys = { git = \"...\", tag = \"v0.2.1\", version = \"0.1.2\" }` and `slop-rdf-sys = { ..., version = \"0.3.0\" }`. Makefile's `crate-vendor` target filters CRATE_SRCS/CRATE_HDRS to exclude SHARED_MODULES and `rm -f`s any stale vendored copies before copying (see the \"No vendoring of slop-std-sys/slop-rdf-sys shared modules\" Constraint this decision is motivated by). rust/build.rs reads `DEP_SLOP_RDF_INCLUDE`/`DEP_SLOP_STD_INCLUDE` (cargo `links` metadata env vars exposed by the two -sys crates) and adds them as include paths, and its `sources` array shrinks from 19 growl+shared files to the 10 growl-only files. .github/workflows/release.yml adds a \"Build and test Rust crate with slop-sys\" step (`make crate-test`) ahead of the release build." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0950df26-7f03-4085-84fb-523dc9b7145a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0950df26-7f03-4085-84fb-523dc9b7145a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/b1330b6d-5bbc-49fa-878a-1d190339714e> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0950df26-7f03-4085-84fb-523dc9b7145a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-10T18:10:28Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0950df26-7f03-4085-84fb-523dc9b7145a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Consume shared C modules via slop-std-sys/slop-rdf-sys" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0950df26-7f03-4085-84fb-523dc9b7145a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isMotivatedBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/49a65175-ddca-419e-9a33-dd3a3fe3b5d9> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0950df26-7f03-4085-84fb-523dc9b7145a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d5a2c63d-8f7f-4013-959a-c3f88e2adf8c> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/12e12e55-e325-490b-aeda-0c5e60151b98> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/12e12e55-e325-490b-aeda-0c5e60151b98> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Adopt OWL 2 RL profile for growl reasoner" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/12e12e55-e325-490b-aeda-0c5e60151b98> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/365040dc-aee8-456c-936c-47a7dbb4c79b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/12e12e55-e325-490b-aeda-0c5e60151b98> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/12e12e55-e325-490b-aeda-0c5e60151b98> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Growl implements the OWL 2 RL profile — rule-based, tractable reasoning per the W3C OWL 2 RL specification — rather than a general OWL DL/tableau reasoner. Evidence: src/growl.slop module doc states \"A Z3-verifiable OWL 2 RL profile reasoner implementing the W3C specification inference rules\"; the five rule modules in src/rules/ are organized directly around OWL 2 RL spec tables (eq=Table 4, prp=Table 5, cls=Table 6, cax=Table 7, scm=Table 9), each citing https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-profiles/#OWL_2_RL." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/12e12e55-e325-490b-aeda-0c5e60151b98> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
