<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/2dedc0f9-53f1-4331-afd1-da069c898528> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/ced3a316-cf9e-4a07-9bb2-09150e47c552> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3100dd1e-a2c5-4f0b-8437-2f9c159d2955> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3100dd1e-a2c5-4f0b-8437-2f9c159d2955> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Tag-triggered GitHub Actions release pipeline" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3100dd1e-a2c5-4f0b-8437-2f9c159d2955> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/74af8f69-d68a-4db6-a495-07bb196e4866> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3100dd1e-a2c5-4f0b-8437-2f9c159d2955> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/b44c8fa6-048b-4f14-b9ec-ecfa5010e5a0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3100dd1e-a2c5-4f0b-8437-2f9c159d2955> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3100dd1e-a2c5-4f0b-8437-2f9c159d2955> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Pushing a `v*` git tag now automatically builds and publishes a GitHub Release for growl, instead of releases being cut and uploaded by hand. The new .github/workflows/release.yml runs a `build` job as a two-way OS/compiler matrix (ubuntu-latest+gcc → linux-x86_64, macos-14+gcc-14 → macos-arm64) that runs `make test`, builds the release CLI via `make release` (renamed to growl-${platform}), then rebuilds clean with release CFLAGS (-O3 -DNDEBUG -DSLOP_ARENA_NO_CAP) and packages the library via the new `make dist PLATFORM=...` target, uploading both the CLI binary and libgrowl-${platform}.zip as per-platform artifacts. A downstream `release` job downloads all artifacts and publishes them via softprops/action-gh-release with `generate_release_notes: true`.\n\nEvidence: new file .github/workflows/release.yml — `on: push: tags: ['v*']`, the `build` job's `strategy.matrix.include` (ubuntu-latest/linux-x86_64/gcc, macos-14/macos-arm64/gcc-14), its steps (`make test`, `make release`, `mv build/growl growl-${{ matrix.platform }}`, `make clean` + `make lib` with release CFLAGS, `make dist PLATFORM=...`), and the `release` job's `actions/download-artifact@v4` + `softprops/action-gh-release@v2` step." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3100dd1e-a2c5-4f0b-8437-2f9c159d2955> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3100dd1e-a2c5-4f0b-8437-2f9c159d2955> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-09T18:52:51Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3100dd1e-a2c5-4f0b-8437-2f9c159d2955> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Tag-triggered GitHub Actions release pipeline" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3100dd1e-a2c5-4f0b-8437-2f9c159d2955> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/9c583e55-2542-4b46-8e6d-112ab87ad576> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/31159318-c5eb-4bcc-8f1e-9f9fa92fcddf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/31159318-c5eb-4bcc-8f1e-9f9fa92fcddf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "CLI reports per-phase parse/reason timing" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/31159318-c5eb-4bcc-8f1e-9f9fa92fcddf> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/e71422b6-0c80-4741-aa68-a27243061168> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/31159318-c5eb-4bcc-8f1e-9f9fa92fcddf> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/31159318-c5eb-4bcc-8f1e-9f9fa92fcddf> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "cli/main.slop now measures and prints wall-clock elapsed time for the TTL-parse phase and the reasoning phase separately, and restructures its success output around those numbers. Evidence: commit 75b17fd diff on cli/main.slop — a new `(ffi \"slop_runtime.h\" (slop_now_ms (() I64)))` binding and a new `print-elapsed` helper (seconds + zero-padded milliseconds) are added; `parse-start`/`parse-elapsed` are threaded around the parse-ttl-file call and `reason-start`/`reason-elapsed` around the reason call; the non-quiet output changes from a `[PASS] Ontology is consistent` line followed by indented `Inferred:`/`Iterations:`/`Total:` lines to `Parsed N triples from <path> (Xs)` followed by `Reasoning completed: N inferred in M iterations (Ys)` and `Total: N triples`." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/31159318-c5eb-4bcc-8f1e-9f9fa92fcddf> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/31159318-c5eb-4bcc-8f1e-9f9fa92fcddf> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-04T23:49:15Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/31159318-c5eb-4bcc-8f1e-9f9fa92fcddf> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "CLI reports per-phase parse/reason timing" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3524af0f-b5bd-4b77-ba99-2526b301d02d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3524af0f-b5bd-4b77-ba99-2526b301d02d> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "CLI --version flag sourced from release-tag-derived GROWL_VERSION" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3524af0f-b5bd-4b77-ba99-2526b301d02d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/74af8f69-d68a-4db6-a495-07bb196e4866> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3524af0f-b5bd-4b77-ba99-2526b301d02d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/b44c8fa6-048b-4f14-b9ec-ecfa5010e5a0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3524af0f-b5bd-4b77-ba99-2526b301d02d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/e71422b6-0c80-4741-aa68-a27243061168> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3524af0f-b5bd-4b77-ba99-2526b301d02d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3524af0f-b5bd-4b77-ba99-2526b301d02d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "growl's CLI now supports `--version`/`-V`, printing `growl &lt;version&gt;` where the version string comes from a `GROWL_VERSION` C preprocessor macro compiled into the binary (Makefile default `GROWL_VERSION ?= 0.1.0`), and the existing tag-triggered release workflow now derives that macro's value from the pushed git tag (stripping the leading \"v\" via `VERSION=${GITHUB_REF_NAME#v}`) and passes it to `make release GROWL_VERSION=$VERSION`, so release binaries report the tag they were actually built from rather than a hardcoded placeholder.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit 4c9f93a450 (\"adding version switch to cli\") — cli/main.slop's CliArgs record gains a `show-version Bool` field and a `--version`/`-V` parse-args branch; main gains `(if (. args show-version) (do (c-inline \"printf(\\\"growl %s\\\\n\\\", GROWL_VERSION)\") 0) ...)` checked before the existing input-file match, with the whole prior body pushed into the `else` branch (mirrored in the regenerated csrc/src/slop_main.c). Makefile adds `GROWL_VERSION ?= 0.1.0` and threads `-DGROWL_VERSION=\\\"$(GROWL_VERSION)\\\"` into both the default and `release:` CFLAGS. .github/workflows/release.yml's \"Build release CLI\" step changes from a bare `make release CC=...` to computing `VERSION=${GITHUB_REF_NAME#v}` and running `make release CC=... GROWL_VERSION=$VERSION`, tying this into the tag-triggered release pipeline recorded separately." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3524af0f-b5bd-4b77-ba99-2526b301d02d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3524af0f-b5bd-4b77-ba99-2526b301d02d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-09T22:00:49Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3524af0f-b5bd-4b77-ba99-2526b301d02d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "CLI --version flag sourced from release-tag-derived GROWL_VERSION" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3524af0f-b5bd-4b77-ba99-2526b301d02d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/2d7b91c8-4a0a-484c-8145-b1eee40760ba> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3df3ff4f-caaf-49ce-b99c-a9f05d8a9571> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3df3ff4f-caaf-49ce-b99c-a9f05d8a9571> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "SLOP_ARENA_NO_CAP build-time arena-cap bypass" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3df3ff4f-caaf-49ce-b99c-a9f05d8a9571> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/74af8f69-d68a-4db6-a495-07bb196e4866> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3df3ff4f-caaf-49ce-b99c-a9f05d8a9571> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3df3ff4f-caaf-49ce-b99c-a9f05d8a9571> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "csrc/runtime/slop_runtime.h's two SLOP_ARENA_MAX_TOTAL_BYTES enforcement checks (in slop_arena_new and the overflow-growth path of slop_arena_alloc) are now wrapped in #ifndef SLOP_ARENA_NO_CAP / #endif, so a build compiled with -DSLOP_ARENA_NO_CAP skips both abort()-on-exceeded-cap checks entirely, while a default build (SLOP_ARENA_NO_CAP left undefined) keeps enforcing the cap exactly as before.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit 403b956ee3 (\"added fast mode, updated README\") diff on csrc/runtime/slop_runtime.h — both `if (atomic_load(&slop_global_allocated) + capacity > SLOP_ARENA_MAX_TOTAL_BYTES) { ...; abort(); }` blocks (one in slop_arena_new, one in slop_arena_alloc's growth path) gain a surrounding `#ifndef SLOP_ARENA_NO_CAP` / `#endif`. No build target in this commit defines SLOP_ARENA_NO_CAP — the Makefile is untouched by this diff — so this is dormant infrastructure at this point in history: an opt-out mechanism added without yet being wired into any build target." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3df3ff4f-caaf-49ce-b99c-a9f05d8a9571> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3df3ff4f-caaf-49ce-b99c-a9f05d8a9571> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-07T07:36:12Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3df3ff4f-caaf-49ce-b99c-a9f05d8a9571> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "SLOP_ARENA_NO_CAP build-time arena-cap bypass" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3df3ff4f-caaf-49ce-b99c-a9f05d8a9571> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/0213903f-546c-416a-a432-312c595b1de2> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3f5e5977-57b0-45a1-8b9a-e544cedfd4ce> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3f5e5977-57b0-45a1-8b9a-e544cedfd4ce> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Semi-naive delta-based fixpoint evaluation" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3f5e5977-57b0-45a1-8b9a-e544cedfd4ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/7a377274-e1bc-43a2-b657-8ae3e39fdefb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3f5e5977-57b0-45a1-8b9a-e544cedfd4ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3f5e5977-57b0-45a1-8b9a-e544cedfd4ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The engine's main loop (engine-run / engine-run-iteration / apply-all-rules in src/engine.slop) applies rules only against the current Delta of newly-derived triples each iteration, then filters out results already present in the graph, rather than re-evaluating all rules over the whole accumulated graph every pass. This is semi-naive Datalog-style evaluation applied to OWL 2 RL rule firing. types.slop's Delta type comment frames this explicitly: \"Designed for future extension to differential dataflow.\" The loop terminates when a fixpoint (empty delta) or config.max-iterations is reached." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3f5e5977-57b0-45a1-8b9a-e544cedfd4ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3f5e5977-57b0-45a1-8b9a-e544cedfd4ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-01-27T01:30:15Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3f5e5977-57b0-45a1-8b9a-e544cedfd4ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Semi-naive delta-based fixpoint evaluation" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3f5e5977-57b0-45a1-8b9a-e544cedfd4ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isSupersededBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8afd2e38-3664-402e-9dbd-30a634c91dc3> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3f5e5977-57b0-45a1-8b9a-e544cedfd4ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b60d9cc3-3836-4d8c-9c71-94f6bceb4bfa> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/46b6eb2f-386e-47d1-82f6-6aed459402e6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/46b6eb2f-386e-47d1-82f6-6aed459402e6> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fork-join parallel rule dispatch" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/46b6eb2f-386e-47d1-82f6-6aed459402e6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/7a377274-e1bc-43a2-b657-8ae3e39fdefb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/46b6eb2f-386e-47d1-82f6-6aed459402e6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/46b6eb2f-386e-47d1-82f6-6aed459402e6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "apply-all-rules now dispatches per iteration instead of always running single-threaded: iteration 0, or any ReasonerConfig with worker-count <= 1, takes apply-all-rules-sequential (the unchanged scm -> cax -> prp -> eq -> cls order); every other iteration with worker-count > 1 takes the new apply-all-rules-parallel, which allocates five coordinator-owned 1MB arenas (arena-scm/cax/prp/eq/cls), spawns one worker thread per rule group via spawn-rule-workers (each worker runs only its own rule group against its own arena and the shared read-only graph/delta), merges results via collect-worker-results, then frees the five worker arenas. Evidence: commit 95c5860 (PR #1 \"thread_it\") diff on src/engine.slop — apply-all-rules gains a ReasonerConfig parameter and the `(if (or (<= (. config worker-count) 1) (== (. delta iteration) 0)) apply-all-rules-sequential apply-all-rules-parallel)` dispatch; the module doc gains \"Each of the 5 rule groups (scm, cax, prp, eq, cls) runs in its own thread with its own arena; results merge on the coordinator thread.\"" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/46b6eb2f-386e-47d1-82f6-6aed459402e6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/46b6eb2f-386e-47d1-82f6-6aed459402e6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-06T04:49:33Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
