<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/475576a4-e707-46a6-bc4b-d6ca77c0c94e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/475576a4-e707-46a6-bc4b-d6ca77c0c94e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Semantic sub-worker partitioning for parallel rule dispatch" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/475576a4-e707-46a6-bc4b-d6ca77c0c94e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/7a377274-e1bc-43a2-b657-8ae3e39fdefb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/475576a4-e707-46a6-bc4b-d6ca77c0c94e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/475576a4-e707-46a6-bc4b-d6ca77c0c94e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Growl's fork-join parallel rule-application phase (apply-all-rules-parallel, spawned from apply-all-rules when config.worker-count > 1 and iteration != 0) now spawns 12 sub-worker threads instead of 5, splitting each of the five OWL 2 RL rule groups into 2-3 semantically-grouped sub-workers that each call a hand-picked subset of that group's individual rule functions directly (rather than the group's apply-*-rules aggregate). This raises the ceiling on available parallelism within a single fixpoint iteration beyond one thread per rule group, presumably in response to running the reasoner against much larger real-world ontologies (this commit also adds Brick.ttl (48827 lines) and schemaorg.ttl (21562 lines) as benchmark fixtures) where a single rule group's work no longer fits comfortably on one thread. The umbrella decision to dispatch iterations > 0 with worker-count > 1 through a parallel fork-join path (vs. the sequential path) is unchanged by this commit — only the worker-partitioning granularity inside that parallel path changes." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/475576a4-e707-46a6-bc4b-d6ca77c0c94e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/475576a4-e707-46a6-bc4b-d6ca77c0c94e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/4664a23f-a3f7-4ac1-a865-b23b7e5958d9> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
