<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4c927d1e-dc84-4d00-8dd1-c95f5bdbc0f3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4c927d1e-dc84-4d00-8dd1-c95f5bdbc0f3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Intern-pool threadsafety + bucket sizing in native build" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4c927d1e-dc84-4d00-8dd1-c95f5bdbc0f3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/74af8f69-d68a-4db6-a495-07bb196e4866> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4c927d1e-dc84-4d00-8dd1-c95f5bdbc0f3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4c927d1e-dc84-4d00-8dd1-c95f5bdbc0f3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The native C build (Makefile default/release CFLAGS) and the GitHub Actions release workflow's library build step now compile with -DSLOP_INTERN_THREADSAFE and a new -DSLOP_INTERN_BUCKET_COUNT=65536, extending the mutex-protected intern pool (see \"Mutex-protected intern pool under SLOP_INTERN_THREADSAFE\") to the Makefile-driven CLI/library/release C build — previously only rust/build.rs defined SLOP_INTERN_THREADSAFE for the Rust crate's C build — and introducing a new build-tunable hash-table bucket count for the intern pool.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit 4bfd631358ff (\"Memory improvements (#17)\", body \"fixes to memory allocation\") diff — .github/workflows/release.yml's release-library build step's CFLAGS gains `-DSLOP_INTERN_THREADSAFE -DSLOP_INTERN_BUCKET_COUNT=65536` alongside the pre-existing `-DSLOP_ARENA_NO_CAP`; Makefile's default CFLAGS (backing the `cli`/`test` targets) and its `release:` target's CFLAGS gain the identical two defines. The diff shown does not include csrc/runtime/slop_runtime.h, so the internal consumer of SLOP_INTERN_BUCKET_COUNT is not directly evidenced here, only its introduction as a build-time knob." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4c927d1e-dc84-4d00-8dd1-c95f5bdbc0f3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4c927d1e-dc84-4d00-8dd1-c95f5bdbc0f3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-04-06T18:27:08Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4c927d1e-dc84-4d00-8dd1-c95f5bdbc0f3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Intern-pool threadsafety + bucket sizing in native build" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4c927d1e-dc84-4d00-8dd1-c95f5bdbc0f3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/47c625fa-b5c3-442a-987c-d2aeb7fe40d4> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5edc6976-18a8-4f07-9d32-aeadb73a4887> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5edc6976-18a8-4f07-9d32-aeadb73a4887> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Extract types.slop to break growl/engine import cycle" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5edc6976-18a8-4f07-9d32-aeadb73a4887> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/bfddb2b9-baed-4f0a-a841-6ce6ff4c9dc0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5edc6976-18a8-4f07-9d32-aeadb73a4887> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5edc6976-18a8-4f07-9d32-aeadb73a4887> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "types.slop was split out because both growl.slop and engine.slop need Delta/EngineState/ReasonerConfig/ReasonerResult/InconsistencyReport, while engine.slop is imported by growl.slop (via engine-run) — a direct cross-import of the shared types would cycle. The module's own header states this rationale explicitly: \"Shared type definitions used by both growl and engine modules. This module breaks the circular dependency.\"" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5edc6976-18a8-4f07-9d32-aeadb73a4887> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5edc6976-18a8-4f07-9d32-aeadb73a4887> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-01-27T01:30:15Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5edc6976-18a8-4f07-9d32-aeadb73a4887> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Extract types.slop to break growl/engine import cycle" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/64832702-061c-4f59-bc38-c41938f8f781> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/64832702-061c-4f59-bc38-c41938f8f781> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Scope README verification claims to enumerated proofs" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/64832702-061c-4f59-bc38-c41938f8f781> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/365040dc-aee8-456c-936c-47a7dbb4c79b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/64832702-061c-4f59-bc38-c41938f8f781> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/64832702-061c-4f59-bc38-c41938f8f781> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "README.md's framing is narrowed from unqualified claims of formal verification — \"An OWL 2 RL reasoner with formally verified inference rules\", \"Formally Verified: All inference rules have Z3-verified pre/post conditions\" — to explicit, enumerated scope: \"Z3-Verified Contracts: Every inference function has machine-checked pre/postconditions; soundness properties prove each output triple is justified by a delta/graph premise\". A new \"## Verification\" subsection states exact counts (55 of 77 inference functions carry a soundness property, 8 carry completeness, 3 carry novelty) and adds a \"What is not proven\" list: soundness is not proven for cls-maxc2/cls-maxqc3/cls-maxqc4 (callback functions that query the full graph rather than iterating delta, so the standard delta-sourcing property doesn't apply); full multi-way join semantics (e.g. cls-int1 checking all intersection components) aren't fully encoded by the delta-sourcing soundness contracts; fixed-point loop termination is not formally proven; and generated-C memory safety is not verified. The `slop verify` usage example is also corrected from listing explicit file globs to the current `slop verify` / `slop verify -v` form driven by slop.toml's [verify].sources. Evidence: commit 535cc1e (PR #5 \"more_contracts\", \"More contracts\") diff hunk on README.md, the Overview/Features/Verification sections." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/64832702-061c-4f59-bc38-c41938f8f781> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/64832702-061c-4f59-bc38-c41938f8f781> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-08T22:15:17Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/64832702-061c-4f59-bc38-c41938f8f781> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Scope README verification claims to enumerated proofs" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/64832702-061c-4f59-bc38-c41938f8f781> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isMotivatedBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/13610b21-6950-4164-85fe-607a21c9bc26> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
