<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6bfc683e-2647-4b78-ab03-e3ebb1ee71f4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6bfc683e-2647-4b78-ab03-e3ebb1ee71f4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Cooperative cancellation via atomic cancel-ptr flag" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6bfc683e-2647-4b78-ab03-e3ebb1ee71f4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/7a377274-e1bc-43a2-b657-8ae3e39fdefb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6bfc683e-2647-4b78-ab03-e3ebb1ee71f4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/9f7a7679-6c17-40b2-bbef-b78d9832bfa1> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6bfc683e-2647-4b78-ab03-e3ebb1ee71f4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/bfddb2b9-baed-4f0a-a841-6ce6ff4c9dc0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6bfc683e-2647-4b78-ab03-e3ebb1ee71f4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/e71422b6-0c80-4741-aa68-a27243061168> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6bfc683e-2647-4b78-ab03-e3ebb1ee71f4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6bfc683e-2647-4b78-ab03-e3ebb1ee71f4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "ReasonerConfig gains a new cancel-ptr I64 field (default 0 = disabled) holding a pointer to a caller-owned atomic flag; engine-run's main fixpoint loop checks it once per iteration via an atomic relaxed load (c-inline `if (config.cancel_ptr && __atomic_load_n((uint32_t*)(uintptr_t)config.cancel_ptr, __ATOMIC_RELAXED)) { done = 1; cancelled = 1; }`) before running that iteration's rules, and halts early without discarding work already inferred. On cancellation, engine-run returns a new third ReasonerResult variant, reason-cancelled, carrying the same ReasonerSuccess payload (graph, inferred-count, iterations) as reason-success, so callers get a well-formed, sound partial result instead of an error or a hang.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit d3bda85a (#18, \"Cancellable operations\"). src/types.slop adds `(cancel-ptr I64)` to ReasonerConfig and a third `(reason-cancelled ReasonerSuccess)` arm to the ReasonerResult union (with comment \"reason-cancelled is returned when a cancel token is triggered mid-reasoning\"). src/engine.slop's engine-run inserts the atomic check at the top of the while-loop body and, when cancelled, returns `(union-new ReasonerResult reason-cancelled (record-new ReasonerSuccess ...))` built from the state reached so far. README.md documents it under Features as \"Cooperative Cancellation: Cancel in-progress reasoning via atomic flag; returns sound partial results\". cli/main.slop adds a `((reason-cancelled s) ...)` report branch printing \"[CANCELLED] Reasoning was cancelled\" plus the partial inferred-count/iterations." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6bfc683e-2647-4b78-ab03-e3ebb1ee71f4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6bfc683e-2647-4b78-ab03-e3ebb1ee71f4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-04-07T04:23:50Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6bfc683e-2647-4b78-ab03-e3ebb1ee71f4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Cooperative cancellation via atomic cancel-ptr flag" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6bfc683e-2647-4b78-ab03-e3ebb1ee71f4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isConstrainedBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/4ae877b4-6766-4663-87dd-91ba8210e76b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6bfc683e-2647-4b78-ab03-e3ebb1ee71f4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/17e0af19-2201-4730-a97b-053446bea4a4> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6c226bae-bfea-43cb-b465-35b2a3f461ba> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6c226bae-bfea-43cb-b465-35b2a3f461ba> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Scoped scratch arenas for transient delta materialization" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6c226bae-bfea-43cb-b465-35b2a3f461ba> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/7a377274-e1bc-43a2-b657-8ae3e39fdefb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6c226bae-bfea-43cb-b465-35b2a3f461ba> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6c226bae-bfea-43cb-b465-35b2a3f461ba> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "engine_engine_run and engine_schema_materialize (csrc/src/slop_engine.c, generated from src/engine.slop) now compute their transient \"full delta\" / \"initial delta\" snapshots inside short-lived scratch arenas that are freed once consumed, instead of allocating them permanently into the long-lived arena passed down from the caller.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit 4bfd631358ff (\"Memory improvements (#17)\", body \"fixes to memory allocation\") diff on csrc/src/slop_engine.c:\n- engine_engine_run now allocates a dedicated 4MB `init_delta_arena` (heap-boxed via malloc + slop_arena_new) up front and threads it through every engine_make_initial_delta(...) call that previously used the caller's long-lived `arena` (initial_delta, the schema-materialize call inside materialized_graph, and the validate-mode fixpoint_delta), then explicitly frees it (slop_arena_free + free) both on the config.validate-and-inconsistent early-return branch and again after the main fixpoint while-loop.\n- engine_schema_materialize's three phases (edges: scm-eqc1/eqc1b/eqp1/eqp1b/int/uni; mutual-eq: scm-eqc2/eqp2; dom/rng: scm-dom1/dom2/rng1/rng2) each wrap their own engine_make_initial_delta(arena, graph) + rule-application block in a new block-local `slop_arena _arena_scratch = slop_arena_new(4194304); slop_arena* scratch = &_arena_scratch;`, using it only for that phase's full_d, then call slop_arena_free(scratch) at the end of the block — replacing the prior scheme where each phase's transient full-delta shared the same long-lived `arena` as the graph triples the phase permanently adds." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6c226bae-bfea-43cb-b465-35b2a3f461ba> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6c226bae-bfea-43cb-b465-35b2a3f461ba> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-04-06T18:27:08Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
