<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6c226bae-bfea-43cb-b465-35b2a3f461ba> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/535cc8ea-1109-4f97-9b6a-b7a14969d03a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6c226bae-bfea-43cb-b465-35b2a3f461ba> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/f7329b46-7dab-4a62-88f0-dc95b892fdd2> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6cb7f398-ac5c-43f0-a62c-828025adc7d5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6cb7f398-ac5c-43f0-a62c-828025adc7d5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fast mode gains scm-sco/scm-eqc1 schema closure" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6cb7f398-ac5c-43f0-a62c-828025adc7d5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/365040dc-aee8-456c-936c-47a7dbb4c79b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6cb7f398-ac5c-43f0-a62c-828025adc7d5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/7a377274-e1bc-43a2-b657-8ae3e39fdefb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6cb7f398-ac5c-43f0-a62c-828025adc7d5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6cb7f398-ac5c-43f0-a62c-828025adc7d5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Growl's `--fast` flag now materializes a targeted schema closure (scm-sco transitive subClassOf closure, plus scm-eqc1/scm-eqc1b equivalentClass->subClassOf) instead of skipping schema materialization entirely, so that `--fast`'s rule coverage matches the `reasonable` reference reasoner used in the benchmark comparison harness. It continues to skip the remaining scm-* rules (scm-op/dp/eqp/int/uni/dom/rng/svf/avf/hv), dt-type1/dt-not-type, eq-diff1/2/3, eq-ref, and cls-maxc1/2/cls-maxqc1-4, and continues to run the consistency-check rules (cax-dw, cax-adc, prp-asyp, prp-irp, prp-pdw, prp-adp, prp-npa1/2, cls-nothing2, cls-com) unconditionally. It deliberately does not replicate Reasonable's non-standard typing of every entity as owl:Thing." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6cb7f398-ac5c-43f0-a62c-828025adc7d5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6cb7f398-ac5c-43f0-a62c-828025adc7d5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/112a81fc-4963-4576-91ac-7ab283fb4d7b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6cb7f398-ac5c-43f0-a62c-828025adc7d5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-29T18:50:33Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6cb7f398-ac5c-43f0-a62c-828025adc7d5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Fast mode gains scm-sco/scm-eqc1 schema closure" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
