<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6f06b5c4-d567-418f-8947-8835bff5d25a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6f06b5c4-d567-418f-8947-8835bff5d25a> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Single-lookup insert for Delta by-predicate map" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6f06b5c4-d567-418f-8947-8835bff5d25a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/bfddb2b9-baed-4f0a-a841-6ce6ff4c9dc0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6f06b5c4-d567-418f-8947-8835bff5d25a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6f06b5c4-d567-418f-8947-8835bff5d25a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "delta-add's population of Delta's by-predicate map now does a single map-get and only creates+inserts a new predicate-set on a miss, instead of an unconditional map-has check followed by an unconditional map-put of an empty set and then a separate map-get.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit 57361a3174 (\"small performance tweak\", src/types.slop, delta-add) replaces `(when (not (map-has pred-map pred)) (map-put pred-map pred (set-new arena Triple))) (match (map-get pred-map pred) ((some pred-set) (set-put pred-set t)) ((none) (do)))` with `(match (map-get pred-map pred) ((some pred-set) (set-put pred-set t)) ((none) (let ((new-set (set-new arena Triple))) (set-put new-set t) (map-put pred-map pred new-set))))`. This is a constant-factor optimization of the by-predicate indexing block introduced by \"Predicate-indexed Delta lookup for rule matching\" (map-has + map-put + map-get collapsed into one map-get with insert-on-miss), removing a redundant hash-map operation from delta-add's hot insert path. The commit does not change the by-predicate indexing design itself (still a Map Term (Set Triple), still populated incrementally inside delta-add) — only this internal lookup pattern." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6f06b5c4-d567-418f-8947-8835bff5d25a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6f06b5c4-d567-418f-8947-8835bff5d25a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-06T21:35:04Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6f06b5c4-d567-418f-8947-8835bff5d25a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Single-lookup insert for Delta by-predicate map" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6f06b5c4-d567-418f-8947-8835bff5d25a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/eeca1158-99ca-4478-82bd-0fad190c57b6> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6f06b5c4-d567-418f-8947-8835bff5d25a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/96300246-01e8-4bff-85c9-7d60914887fa> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6fd048e0-d0c8-4e3d-91b4-091023a07e0f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6fd048e0-d0c8-4e3d-91b4-091023a07e0f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Release CI matrix runs with fail-fast disabled" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6fd048e0-d0c8-4e3d-91b4-091023a07e0f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/b44c8fa6-048b-4f14-b9ec-ecfa5010e5a0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6fd048e0-d0c8-4e3d-91b4-091023a07e0f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6fd048e0-d0c8-4e3d-91b4-091023a07e0f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "growl's release.yml build job's matrix strategy now sets `fail-fast: false`, so a compile failure on one platform (e.g. macOS/gcc-14) no longer cancels the other in-flight matrix job (e.g. ubuntu/gcc) — each platform now runs to completion and reports its own pass/fail status independently, instead of one platform's failure hiding the other's result.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit cf8aaf7260 (\"fix macOS release build: use pthread_t for thread ID fields\") adds `fail-fast: false` to .github/workflows/release.yml's `build.strategy`, in the same commit that fixes a macOS-only hard compiler error (pthread_t vs uint64_t under GCC 14) — bundling a CI-visibility fix alongside the platform-specific build fix it was masking." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6fd048e0-d0c8-4e3d-91b4-091023a07e0f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6fd048e0-d0c8-4e3d-91b4-091023a07e0f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-09T22:31:23Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6fd048e0-d0c8-4e3d-91b4-091023a07e0f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Release CI matrix runs with fail-fast disabled" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7acb36f2-0ee0-4da9-81a1-5ab13296b00c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7acb36f2-0ee0-4da9-81a1-5ab13296b00c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Inconsistency reported as typed Result, not exception" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7acb36f2-0ee0-4da9-81a1-5ab13296b00c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/7a377274-e1bc-43a2-b657-8ae3e39fdefb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7acb36f2-0ee0-4da9-81a1-5ab13296b00c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/bfddb2b9-baed-4f0a-a841-6ce6ff4c9dc0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7acb36f2-0ee0-4da9-81a1-5ab13296b00c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7acb36f2-0ee0-4da9-81a1-5ab13296b00c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "ReasonerResult is a union of reason-success (ReasonerSuccess: graph + inferred-count + iterations) and reason-inconsistent (InconsistencyReport: reason string + witness triples), defined in src/types.slop. Rule application threads (Result Delta InconsistencyReport) through apply-all-rules / apply-*-rules and the engine loop, so an OWL inconsistency (e.g. a disjoint-class violation) is surfaced as typed data the caller must match on, carrying witness triples for diagnosis, instead of being thrown as an error/panic." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7acb36f2-0ee0-4da9-81a1-5ab13296b00c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7acb36f2-0ee0-4da9-81a1-5ab13296b00c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-01-27T01:30:15Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7acb36f2-0ee0-4da9-81a1-5ab13296b00c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Inconsistency reported as typed Result, not exception" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7b7344a7-2437-4975-a59e-7c963dc91b03> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7b7344a7-2437-4975-a59e-7c963dc91b03> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Update slop-rdf for indexing and parsing performance" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7b7344a7-2437-4975-a59e-7c963dc91b03> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/74af8f69-d68a-4db6-a495-07bb196e4866> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7b7344a7-2437-4975-a59e-7c963dc91b03> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/7a377274-e1bc-43a2-b657-8ae3e39fdefb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7b7344a7-2437-4975-a59e-7c963dc91b03> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7b7344a7-2437-4975-a59e-7c963dc91b03> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Growl's vendored slop-rdf dependency is bumped specifically for a performance increase, adding two concrete optimizations visible in the regenerated C: (1) IndexedGraph's TripleIndex gains a fourth `pos` (predicate→object→subject) permutation map alongside the existing spo/pso/osp, so a lookup with a bound predicate+object and unbound subject resolves via a direct `pos[p][o]` hash lookup instead of falling back through `pso` and linearly scanning every subject bucket under that predicate to test object-set membership; and (2) the TTL parser's char-skipping loops (e.g. common_skip_whitespace) now track offset/line/column as local scalars through the loop and construct the ParseState once via a new `common_state_with_position` constructor, instead of calling `common_state_advance` (which reallocates/copies a ParseState) once per character. Every other touched file (slop_cax.c, slop_cls.c, slop_eq.c, slop_prp.c, slop_scm.c, etc.) shows only the mechanical lambda/temp-var renumbering already established as the signature of a slop-rdf regeneration (see \"Adopt RDF 1.2 quoted triple terms from slop-rdf\"), not further functional changes.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit 84bd3aed29939cf25346325d3fb9f6a778fd6d1f (#20 \"Performance improvements\": \"update slop-rdf\" / \"integrate slop-rdf update for perf increase\" / \"update growl.h\") touches 24 files, all under csrc/src/ or generated (include/growl.h) plus README.md/growl_benchmarks.txt — no src/*.slop source changed, and growl's own src/ tree has no index.slop or ttl.slop (confirmed via `git ls-tree`), consistent with this C being transpiled from the vendored ../slop-rdf library. csrc/src/slop_index.h adds `slop_map* pos;` to `struct index_TripleIndex`; slop_index.c's rdf_indexed_graph_create/rdf_indexed_graph_add/rdf_indexed_graph_match are rewritten to populate and query it. csrc/src/slop_common.h/.c add `common_state_with_position(state, offset, line, column)` and rewrite common_skip_whitespace's body to loop over local offset/line/column scalars instead of repeated common_state_advance calls. README.md's Performance table (same commit) shows the resulting wall-clock drop measured in a single pass on one machine, e.g. CCO: Growl --complete 3.1s→462ms, Growl 2.8s→277ms, Growl --fast 434ms→59ms; Brick: Growl --fast 2.3s→98ms; BFO: Growl --fast 3ms→1ms." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7b7344a7-2437-4975-a59e-7c963dc91b03> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7b7344a7-2437-4975-a59e-7c963dc91b03> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-29T17:11:16Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
