<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7b7344a7-2437-4975-a59e-7c963dc91b03> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/a23f9fc4-7a6c-41b2-aa31-997f66d5faf0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7b7344a7-2437-4975-a59e-7c963dc91b03> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/c698fa83-bb8f-4c9f-a344-37afcbc342a4> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7b7344a7-2437-4975-a59e-7c963dc91b03> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/c78fa5a3-2f0d-414c-8234-90dc258dcba9> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7ec9d374-b459-40de-b6b3-d48ab32195d6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7ec9d374-b459-40de-b6b3-d48ab32195d6> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Ship growl as a C-ABI static library" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7ec9d374-b459-40de-b6b3-d48ab32195d6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/9f7a7679-6c17-40b2-bbef-b78d9832bfa1> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7ec9d374-b459-40de-b6b3-d48ab32195d6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7ec9d374-b459-40de-b6b3-d48ab32195d6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "slop.toml's [build] section sets type=\"static\" with output build/libgrowl.a, and every function in growl's public API (src/growl.slop) carries a :c-name annotation (growl_reason, growl_reason_with_config, growl_default_config, growl_is_consistent, growl_get_types, growl_get_same_as, growl_get_inferred_count). This establishes growl's public surface as a C-callable static library meant to be linked into a host application/runtime, rather than a standalone executable." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7ec9d374-b459-40de-b6b3-d48ab32195d6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7ec9d374-b459-40de-b6b3-d48ab32195d6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-01-27T01:30:15Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7ec9d374-b459-40de-b6b3-d48ab32195d6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Ship growl as a C-ABI static library" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7f933cd6-6d43-46ef-b51b-c5ebf84ed4b8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7f933cd6-6d43-46ef-b51b-c5ebf84ed4b8> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Opt-in fast reasoning mode (--fast)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7f933cd6-6d43-46ef-b51b-c5ebf84ed4b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/365040dc-aee8-456c-936c-47a7dbb4c79b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7f933cd6-6d43-46ef-b51b-c5ebf84ed4b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/7a377274-e1bc-43a2-b657-8ae3e39fdefb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7f933cd6-6d43-46ef-b51b-c5ebf84ed4b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/bfddb2b9-baed-4f0a-a841-6ce6ff4c9dc0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7f933cd6-6d43-46ef-b51b-c5ebf84ed4b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/e71422b6-0c80-4741-aa68-a27243061168> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7f933cd6-6d43-46ef-b51b-c5ebf84ed4b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7f933cd6-6d43-46ef-b51b-c5ebf84ed4b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "New ReasonerConfig.fast Bool field (default false) and a CLI --fast/-f flag skip OWL 2 RL schema-vocabulary rules (scm-*) entirely and skip consistency/cardinality checks (cax-dw, cax-adc, prp-asyp, prp-irp, prp-pdw, eq-diff1/2/3, cls-nothing2, cls-com, cls-maxc1/2), matching the inference depth of reasoners like `reasonable` that skip schema closure.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit 403b956ee3 (\"added fast mode, updated README\"). README.md adds a \"Fast Mode\" section: \"--fast skips schema vocabulary rules (scm-*), consistency checks (cax-dw, cax-adc, prp-asyp, prp-irp, prp-pdw, eq-diff1/2/3, cls-nothing2, cls-com), and cardinality rules (cls-maxc1/2)... Most published ontologies already include explicit subClassOf/subPropertyOf chains, making schema closure unnecessary for practical use.\" src/types.slop's ReasonerConfig record gains (fast Bool); src/growl.slop's default-config sets it false. cli/main.slop adds --fast/-f parsing and threads args.fast into the ReasonerConfig built for reason-with-config. src/engine.slop's apply-all-rules-sequential wraps its apply-scm-rules call in (when (not fast) ...) so schema rules are skipped entirely (not per-rule-gated), and threads a new `fast` parameter into apply-cax-rules/apply-prp-rules/apply-eq-rules/apply-cls-rules. Each rule dispatcher (src/rules/cax.slop, prp.slop, eq.slop, cls.slop) wraps only its own consistency-check (and, for cls, cardinality-rule) calls in (when (not fast) ...); non-consistency inference rules (cax-sco, cax-eqc1/2; cls-int1/2, cls-uni, cls-svf1/2, cls-avf, cls-hv1/2, cls-oo, etc.) still run in fast mode. The parallel path (apply-all-rules-parallel / spawn-rule-workers) mirrors this: the 3 scm sub-workers and the cax-check/prp-check/eq-check sub-workers are only spawned when not fast, and their coordinator arenas shrink from 1MB to a 64-byte placeholder in fast mode." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7f933cd6-6d43-46ef-b51b-c5ebf84ed4b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7f933cd6-6d43-46ef-b51b-c5ebf84ed4b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-07T07:36:12Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
