<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8e4dae4e-1737-46b7-a80a-6e9d8136c55c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Migrate growl to SLOP 0.3.0 and slop-sys 0.3.0/0.4.0" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8e4dae4e-1737-46b7-a80a-6e9d8136c55c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/74af8f69-d68a-4db6-a495-07bb196e4866> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8e4dae4e-1737-46b7-a80a-6e9d8136c55c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/833a482a-9217-4511-99e7-1166a8c28fbb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8e4dae4e-1737-46b7-a80a-6e9d8136c55c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/b44c8fa6-048b-4f14-b9ec-ecfa5010e5a0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8e4dae4e-1737-46b7-a80a-6e9d8136c55c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/bfddb2b9-baed-4f0a-a841-6ce6ff4c9dc0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8e4dae4e-1737-46b7-a80a-6e9d8136c55c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8e4dae4e-1737-46b7-a80a-6e9d8136c55c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Growl now builds on SLOP 0.3.0. csrc/ is regenerated with it, the Rust crate depends on slop-std-sys 0.3.0 and slop-rdf-sys 0.4.0, and CI installs SLOP v0.3.0.\n\nWhy + evidence:\n- SLOP 0.3.0 makes an unmarked parameter read-only (slop #180). The only type error in growl was types.slop delta-add pushing onto (. d triples) of its `d` parameter. The fix is `(mut d Delta)`, the same as slop-rdf commit f77c0b2 did for graph-add. The generated C is byte-identical. delta-merge also gained `(@loop-invariant {(. result iteration) == (. d1 iteration)})` so Z3 can prove its postcondition across the for-each.\n- The regenerated csrc differs from the prior tree only in slop_cls.c. Under 0.3.0, a `mut` let captured by a closure (first_val / first_qualified in the cls-maxc/maxqc rules) is captured by pointer (`slop_option_rdf_Term*`) instead of by value. For growl the behavior is the same, because indexed-graph-for-each runs synchronously and the outer local is never read afterwards.\n- rust/Cargo.toml moves from tag v0.2.1 to tag slop-std-sys-v0.3.0 (80e4fcd), which carries both slop-std-sys 0.3.0 and slop-rdf-sys 0.4.0. Every shared-module header, and slop_runtime.h, is byte-identical to growl's regenerated csrc. The .c files differ only in renumbered temporaries, so the FFI ABI matches.\n- Verified with make cli, make test (25/25), make example-test (7 files, 0 unrunnable/unchecked), make conformance (92), make reference (5), make crate-test (41 incl. layout guard), and slop verify src/types.slop (5/5)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8e4dae4e-1737-46b7-a80a-6e9d8136c55c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8e4dae4e-1737-46b7-a80a-6e9d8136c55c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-09-28T18:10:43.826532Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
