<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8fef3fb8-4281-4f7a-90f3-66558fd98861> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/48728664-41b4-4abe-8163-cbcd4d38b602> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/936b0242-4d2d-4a63-ab18-cc1487241b43> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/936b0242-4d2d-4a63-ab18-cc1487241b43> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Opt-in --complete mode plus partial dt-* validation" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/936b0242-4d2d-4a63-ab18-cc1487241b43> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/365040dc-aee8-456c-936c-47a7dbb4c79b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/936b0242-4d2d-4a63-ab18-cc1487241b43> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/e71422b6-0c80-4741-aa68-a27243061168> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/936b0242-4d2d-4a63-ab18-cc1487241b43> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/936b0242-4d2d-4a63-ab18-cc1487241b43> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Growl now implements prp-ap, cls-thing, and cls-nothing1 (Tables 5-6, gated behind a new opt-in `--complete`/`-c` CLI flag) and dt-type1 plus dt-not-type (Table 8, enabled unconditionally), reaching 75/78 OWL 2 RL rules (96%); dt-type2, dt-eq, and dt-diff remain unimplemented.\n\nEvidence: README.md's Rule Coverage table changes prp-* 19/20→20/20, cls-* 17/19→19/19, dt-* 0/5→2/5 (total 70/78→75/78). A new \"Complete Mode\" section: \"The --complete flag enables axiom rules that are skipped by default for performance: cls-thing ... cls-nothing1 ... prp-ap ... These rules are spec-correct but produce triples with zero practical inference value. Use --complete for conformance testing against other reasoners like owlrl.\" Table 8 rows: dt-type1 ✅ \"Assert all OWL 2 datatypes as rdfs:Datatype (36 types)\"; dt-not-type ✅ \"Detect invalid lexical forms (e.g. \\\"abc\\\"^^xsd:integer)\"; dt-type2/dt-eq/dt-diff remain ❌, with dt-eq/dt-diff annotated \"even owlrl skips\". cli/main.slop adds a `complete Bool` CLI-args field and `-c`/`--complete` flag wired into ReasonerConfig (functions dt-type1, dt-not-type in src/rules/dt.slop; cls-thing, cls-nothing1 in src/rules/cls.slop; prp-ap in src/rules/prp.slop). --fast's skip list is also extended to include dt-type1 and dt-not-type. A new fixture cli/tests/fixtures/invalid-literal.ttl (\"abc\"^^xsd:integer) tests dt-not-type, and benchmark_compare.py gains a --diff mode plus --complete support to compare growl's --complete output against OWL-RL as ground truth." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/936b0242-4d2d-4a63-ab18-cc1487241b43> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
