<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9d014455-0149-4886-b44a-707f8e9ee671> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9d014455-0149-4886-b44a-707f8e9ee671> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Split SLOP_LIST_DEFINE into DECLARE + IMPL macros" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9d014455-0149-4886-b44a-707f8e9ee671> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/74af8f69-d68a-4db6-a495-07bb196e4866> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9d014455-0149-4886-b44a-707f8e9ee671> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9d014455-0149-4886-b44a-707f8e9ee671> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The generic list-type macro SLOP_LIST_DEFINE(T, Name) in csrc/runtime/slop_runtime.h is split into two: SLOP_LIST_DECLARE(T, Name) emits only the `{len, cap, T* data}` struct typedef (safe with an incomplete T, since it only stores a pointer), while SLOP_LIST_IMPL(T, Name) emits the `_new`/`_push`/`_get` inline functions (which need sizeof(T), so T must be complete by that point). SLOP_LIST_DEFINE is kept as a convenience macro expanding to SLOP_LIST_DECLARE + SLOP_LIST_IMPL, so every existing call site (SLOP_LIST_DEFINE(int64_t, slop_list_int), etc.) is unaffected.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit 9df6bffce5 diff on csrc/runtime/slop_runtime.h adds the comments \"SLOP_LIST_DECLARE: struct only — safe with incomplete element types (uses T*)\" and \"SLOP_LIST_IMPL: inline functions — requires sizeof(T), so T must be complete\", splitting what was one macro body into SLOP_LIST_DECLARE + SLOP_LIST_IMPL, then redefines SLOP_LIST_DEFINE as their composition. No call site in this diff or at current HEAD uses SLOP_LIST_DECLARE/SLOP_LIST_IMPL directly (grep across csrc/ finds only the definitions themselves) — this lands as dormant infrastructure staged ahead of a not-yet-written consumer that needs a list-of-incomplete-type forward declaration, the same staging-ahead-of-use pattern as the earlier \"Ordered XSD value comparison added as dormant infrastructure\" commit." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9d014455-0149-4886-b44a-707f8e9ee671> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9d014455-0149-4886-b44a-707f8e9ee671> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-11T19:58:48Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/9d014455-0149-4886-b44a-707f8e9ee671> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Split SLOP_LIST_DEFINE into DECLARE + IMPL macros" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a629f09f-c08e-479e-b13d-aad62f5d7136> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a629f09f-c08e-479e-b13d-aad62f5d7136> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Ship growl as a standalone CLI executable" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a629f09f-c08e-479e-b13d-aad62f5d7136> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/9f7a7679-6c17-40b2-bbef-b78d9832bfa1> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a629f09f-c08e-479e-b13d-aad62f5d7136> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/e71422b6-0c80-4741-aa68-a27243061168> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a629f09f-c08e-479e-b13d-aad62f5d7136> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a629f09f-c08e-479e-b13d-aad62f5d7136> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Growl now ships a separate command-line executable (cli/main.slop, cli/slop.toml with type=\"executable\", output build/growl) in addition to the existing C-ABI static library (src/growl.slop). The CLI's main function (:c-name \"main\", argc/argv) parses a TTL file, converts it to an IndexedGraph, calls the library's reason function, and reports consistency/inferred counts, with --quiet and --emit/-o flags. This is a new, additional consumer of the reasoner, not a replacement for the static-library packaging. Evidence: commit c12cd0ed (\"getting bfo test working\") adds cli/main.slop in full (193 lines) with parse-args, print-usage, and a main entry point driving parse-ttl-file -> reason -> serialize-ttl-file." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a629f09f-c08e-479e-b13d-aad62f5d7136> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a629f09f-c08e-479e-b13d-aad62f5d7136> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-03T15:29:45Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a629f09f-c08e-479e-b13d-aad62f5d7136> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Ship growl as a standalone CLI executable" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a6a2f81d-fe4c-4da2-9b75-938a173ff050> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a6a2f81d-fe4c-4da2-9b75-938a173ff050> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Term-only leaf sets in IndexedGraph's SPO/PSO/OSP indexes" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a6a2f81d-fe4c-4da2-9b75-938a173ff050> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/7a377274-e1bc-43a2-b657-8ae3e39fdefb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a6a2f81d-fe4c-4da2-9b75-938a173ff050> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a6a2f81d-fe4c-4da2-9b75-938a173ff050> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "IndexedGraph's three permutation indexes (spo, pso, osp), each a two-level nested map keyed by the first two triple positions, now store a `Set<Term>` of just the third (differentiating) term at the leaf level instead of a `Set<Triple>` of full triple structs — since the first two positions are already implied by which two map levels were walked to reach that leaf, storing the complete Triple there duplicated already-known subject/predicate (or subject/object, or predicate/object) data on every entry. rdf_indexed_graph_add/contains/match/for_each/subjects/objects are all rewritten to reconstruct the full Triple on demand (`(rdf_Triple){.subject = s, .predicate = p, .object = o}`) from the two known outer keys plus the leaf term, rather than reading a stored Triple back out. As a side effect, bound-position lookups in match/for_each/contains change from an O(leaf-set-size) scan-and-filter (`for each stored triple, check rdf_term_eq against the target`) to an O(1) `slop_map_get(term_set, &target) != NULL` lookup.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit cd0f8210dd (#19, \"Improvements for memory usage\") diff on csrc/src/slop_index.c/.h — every leaf-set allocation changes from `slop_map_new_ptr(arena, 16, sizeof(rdf_Triple), slop_hash_rdf_Triple, slop_eq_rdf_Triple)` storing `&(t)` to `slop_map_new_ptr(arena, 16, sizeof(rdf_Term), slop_hash_rdf_Term, slop_eq_rdf_Term)` storing just `&(o)` (spo/pso leaves) or `&(p)` (osp leaves); rdf_indexed_graph_contains/match/for_each's leaf-set scans are replaced with direct map-get lookups or single-field iteration reconstructing the Triple inline. slop_index.h renames the `index_TripleSet`/`index_TripleMap` typedefs to `index_TermSet`/`index_TermSetMap` and drops its now-unused `RDF_TRIPLE_HASH_EQ_DEFINED` hash/eq boilerplate block — that block reappears instead in csrc/src/slop_engine.h, needed there because engine_make_initial_delta now builds a `Map Term (Set Triple)` by-predicate index directly (see \"Batch-construct initial Delta, skip seen-set population\") and hashes/compares `rdf_Triple` values itself.\n\nNote: this repo's src/ tree has no tracked `index.slop` — the `index` module (IndexedGraph, TripleIndex) is resolved from outside growl's own source via the SLOP module resolver, not authored in this repo. This record is grounded directly in the generated-C evidence at csrc/src/slop_index.c/.h, per \"Growl C Build Pipeline\"'s own description of csrc/src/ as generated \"from the .slop originals via slop's module resolver.\"" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a6a2f81d-fe4c-4da2-9b75-938a173ff050> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a6a2f81d-fe4c-4da2-9b75-938a173ff050> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-04-13T03:04:30Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
