<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a6a2f81d-fe4c-4da2-9b75-938a173ff050> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/68f81c10-35f3-4a1a-a467-3172c361372f> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/aa889af0-8778-4919-834e-6a4859e7641b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/aa889af0-8778-4919-834e-6a4859e7641b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Adopt MOOSEDev graph-first project memory" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/aa889af0-8778-4919-834e-6a4859e7641b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/aa889af0-8778-4919-834e-6a4859e7641b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "growl adopts the MOOSEDev MCP server's typed project knowledge graph as the source of truth for architectural decisions, lessons, constraints, requirements, and patterns, rather than free-text notes (e.g. tasks/lessons.md, tasks/todo.md) — those remain optional, human-readable, non-canonical mirrors. This establishes a recall → capture → align → correct → validate workflow for future work: `get_relevant_context` (list-all first, then topic probes) before non-trivial work; `record_important_decision` to capture durable knowledge with rationale and rejected alternatives; `align_concepts` before coining new terms; `supersede_decision`/`retract_decision` instead of duplicating; `validate_against_architecture` after writes. It also codifies general development practices: Plan Mode Default for 3+ step or architectural tasks, liberal subagent use to protect main context, a self-improvement loop that records a Lesson after any user correction, verification before marking work done, pausing to consider simpler designs on non-trivial changes, and autonomous bug fixing without unnecessary context-switching.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit c9a80f902b adds a new root CLAUDE.md (107 lines, the MOOSEDev project-CLAUDE.md template) stating \"This project uses the MOOSEDev MCP server for durable, structured, long-term memory. The typed project knowledge graph is the source of truth ... Free-text notes ... are optional human-readable mirrors, never canonical,\" plus the five-step workflow, tool-selection ladder, and capture-kinds sections; .gitignore adds `.claude/`, `.codex/`, `.mcp.json`, `.moosedev/`, `!./moosedev/kg.nq` so the store's canonical graph text is tracked while local server state is not." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/aa889af0-8778-4919-834e-6a4859e7641b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
