<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b2864e44-41f2-4a36-a993-f2ca470d1f0d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b2864e44-41f2-4a36-a993-f2ca470d1f0d> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Config-gated per-rule-group timing replaces raw memory debug prints" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b2864e44-41f2-4a36-a993-f2ca470d1f0d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/365040dc-aee8-456c-936c-47a7dbb4c79b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b2864e44-41f2-4a36-a993-f2ca470d1f0d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/7a377274-e1bc-43a2-b657-8ae3e39fdefb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b2864e44-41f2-4a36-a993-f2ca470d1f0d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/9f7a7679-6c17-40b2-bbef-b78d9832bfa1> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b2864e44-41f2-4a36-a993-f2ca470d1f0d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/bfddb2b9-baed-4f0a-a841-6ce6ff4c9dc0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b2864e44-41f2-4a36-a993-f2ca470d1f0d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b2864e44-41f2-4a36-a993-f2ca470d1f0d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Engine and scm-rule debug instrumentation switches from unconditional C-level stderr prints of allocated memory (MB) after each rule group / fixpoint iteration to a portable, opt-in per-rule-group wall-clock timing report, gated by a new `ReasonerConfig.verbose` field.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit d9ac429913 (\"print timing info\") diff on src/engine.slop — apply-all-rules-sequential now wraps each of apply-scm-rules/apply-cax-rules/apply-prp-rules/apply-eq-rules/apply-cls-rules with `(let ((t0 (now-ms))) ... (when verbose (do (print \"  scm: \") (print-ms arena (- (now-ms) t0)) (println \"\"))) ...)`, replacing prior lines like `(c-inline \"fprintf(stderr, \\\"  [seq] before scm: %zu MB\\\\n\\\", (size_t)(slop_global_allocated / (1024*1024)))\")`. A new `print-ms` helper (`@intent \"Print a millisecond duration like '12ms'\"`) is added to engine.slop's exports. spawn-rule-workers gains a `verbose Bool` parameter threaded into each of its 5 spawned worker closures for the same per-worker timing print. The top-level fixpoint loop's `(c-inline \"fprintf(stderr, \\\"[engine] iter=%lld graph=%lld global_alloc=%zu MB\\\\n\\\", ...)\")` is replaced by `(when (. config verbose) (do (print \"[iter \") (print (int-to-string arena (. state iteration))) (print \"] graph=\") (print (int-to-string arena (indexed-graph-size (. state graph)))) (println \"\")))`, which reports iteration/graph-size but drops the global_alloc MB figure. src/rules/scm.slop drops its five internal `c-inline fprintf` \"before/after <rule>\" memory-tracking lines with no replacement instrumentation. src/types.slop's ReasonerConfig record gains a `verbose Bool` field; src/growl.slop's default-config sets it to `true` (its @post and @example annotations updated to match, e.g. `@example () -> (ReasonerConfig 4 256 1000 true)`)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b2864e44-41f2-4a36-a993-f2ca470d1f0d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b2864e44-41f2-4a36-a993-f2ca470d1f0d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-07T00:39:15Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b2864e44-41f2-4a36-a993-f2ca470d1f0d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Config-gated per-rule-group timing replaces raw memory debug prints" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b2864e44-41f2-4a36-a993-f2ca470d1f0d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/1321de97-055b-4a9b-9477-15d61fdc9423> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b5c132c4-4584-44fe-b2cc-a9d58c885b7d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b5c132c4-4584-44fe-b2cc-a9d58c885b7d> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Mutex-protected intern pool under SLOP_INTERN_THREADSAFE" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b5c132c4-4584-44fe-b2cc-a9d58c885b7d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/833a482a-9217-4511-99e7-1166a8c28fbb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b5c132c4-4584-44fe-b2cc-a9d58c885b7d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b5c132c4-4584-44fe-b2cc-a9d58c885b7d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Growl's C runtime's global intern pool (slop_global_intern_pool) is now internally synchronized with a pthread_mutex_t (lazily initialized once via pthread_once), compiled in only when SLOP_INTERN_THREADSAFE is defined; rust/build.rs now always defines this flag for the Rust crate's C build, so slop_intern_string is safe to call concurrently from multiple threads without external caller-side locking.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit 1261ab1b2b (merge PR #8 \"thread_safety_fix\", \"minor fix\") diff on csrc/runtime/slop_runtime.h — slop_intern_pool gains a `pthread_mutex_t lock` field (guarded by #ifdef SLOP_INTERN_THREADSAFE); a new `slop_intern_pool_init_impl` + `pthread_once_t slop_intern_once` replaces the lazy-init check for the threadsafe build variant; slop_intern_string wraps its bucket lookup/insert critical section in `pthread_mutex_lock(&slop_global_intern_pool->lock)` / `pthread_mutex_unlock(...)` on both the found-existing and inserted-new return paths. rust/build.rs adds `.define(\"SLOP_INTERN_THREADSAFE\", None)` alongside the existing SLOP_ARENA_NO_CAP define." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b5c132c4-4584-44fe-b2cc-a9d58c885b7d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b5c132c4-4584-44fe-b2cc-a9d58c885b7d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-09T07:10:05Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
