<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b8cdb70b-4db4-4896-961d-93947f3e79a5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b8cdb70b-4db4-4896-961d-93947f3e79a5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Check in generated growl.h as the distributed public C header" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b8cdb70b-4db4-4896-961d-93947f3e79a5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/9f7a7679-6c17-40b2-bbef-b78d9832bfa1> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b8cdb70b-4db4-4896-961d-93947f3e79a5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/b44c8fa6-048b-4f14-b9ec-ecfa5010e5a0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b8cdb70b-4db4-4896-961d-93947f3e79a5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b8cdb70b-4db4-4896-961d-93947f3e79a5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "growl.h — the FFI header the SLOP toolchain generates from src/growl.slop's :c-name-annotated public API (opaque arena/map types, rdf_Term/rdf_Triple/rdf_Graph and friends, the growl_reason*/growl_is_consistent/growl_get_* declarations) — is now checked into the repo at include/growl.h and shipped in the library release archive, rather than being purely an ephemeral `slop build` output that Rust's hand-written ffi.rs had to mirror by hand.\n\nThe Makefile gains a `slop-build` target (`slop build` then `cp build/growl.h include/growl.h`) to refresh it, and a `dist` target that assembles dist/include/{growl.h, csrc/runtime/slop_runtime.h} + dist/lib/libgrowl.a and zips them as libgrowl-$(PLATFORM).zip — so external C consumers of the static library get both the generated public API header and the runtime header it depends on, packaged alongside the .a.\n\nEvidence: new file include/growl.h (243 lines, header comment \"growl.h - Auto-generated FFI header. Do not edit.\"); Makefile diff adds `slop-build: slop build; cp build/growl.h include/growl.h` and `dist: ... cp include/growl.h dist/include/; cp csrc/runtime/slop_runtime.h dist/include/; cp $(BIN)/libgrowl.a dist/lib/; cd dist && zip -r ../libgrowl-$(PLATFORM).zip include/ lib/`." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b8cdb70b-4db4-4896-961d-93947f3e79a5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b8cdb70b-4db4-4896-961d-93947f3e79a5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-09T18:52:51Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
