<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/bafb2a7c-bddb-4435-8af6-d8dd486b144f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/e71422b6-0c80-4741-aa68-a27243061168> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/bafb2a7c-bddb-4435-8af6-d8dd486b144f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/bafb2a7c-bddb-4435-8af6-d8dd486b144f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Growl's `--fast` flag no longer skips the consistency-check rules cax-dw, cax-adc, prp-asyp, prp-irp, prp-pdw, prp-adp, prp-npa1, prp-npa2, cls-nothing2, and cls-com -- these now run unconditionally regardless of the fast flag. `--fast` still skips scm-* (schema vocabulary), dt-type1, dt-not-type, the equality-difference checks eq-diff1/2/3 and eq-ref, and the cardinality rules cls-maxc1/2 and cls-maxqc1-4.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit d54cf78 (merge PR #7 from Trivyn/dttype2, \"Fixing up rust wrapper\"). README.md's Fast Mode paragraph changes from listing cax-dw/cax-adc/prp-asyp/prp-irp/prp-pdw/prp-adp/prp-npa1/prp-npa2/eq-diff1-3/cls-nothing2/cls-com/cls-maxqc1-2 as all skipped, to: \"The --fast flag skips schema vocabulary rules (scm-*), datatype rules (dt-type1, dt-not-type), equality-difference checks (eq-diff1/2/3), eq-ref, and cardinality rules (cls-maxc1/2, cls-maxqc1-4). Consistency checks (cax-dw, cax-adc, prp-asyp, prp-irp, prp-pdw, prp-adp, prp-npa1/2, cls-nothing2, cls-com) still run in fast mode, matching the coverage of reasoners like [reasonable](https://github.com/gtfierro/reasonable).\" Confirmed in generated code: csrc/src/slop_cax.c's cax_apply_cax_rules previously wrapped both its cax_cax_dw and cax_cax_adc calls in `if (!(fast)) { ... }`; this commit removes that guard so both calls execute unconditionally. Confirmed at HEAD: src/rules/cax.slop's apply-cax-rules (line 207) now gates cax-dw/cax-adc only on `(when (not validate) ...)` (line 229), with no `fast` parameter in that gate at all." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
