<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d034f76d-5c48-4ee6-9fbe-9a22806f21e0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d034f76d-5c48-4ee6-9fbe-9a22806f21e0> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rust bindings surface TBox validation mode" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d034f76d-5c48-4ee6-9fbe-9a22806f21e0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/833a482a-9217-4511-99e7-1166a8c28fbb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d034f76d-5c48-4ee6-9fbe-9a22806f21e0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d034f76d-5c48-4ee6-9fbe-9a22806f21e0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The Rust wrapper crate (rust/) now documents/exposes growl's TBox-validation feature — previously CLI-only per \"TBox validation mode via synthetic instance injection\" — as first-class Rust API: `Reasoner::validate()`/`validate_ns(prefix)`, free functions `growl::validate(&arena, &graph)`/`validate_with_ns(...)`, `ReasonerConfig::validate(bool)`/`validate_ns(&str)` builder methods, and matching `ValidateReport`/`ValidateResult`/`OwnedValidateReport`/`OwnedValidateResult` types (entity + reason + witnesses, mirroring InconsistencyReport's shape but per-entity). A `Reasoner::new().complete(true)` convenience builder is also newly documented alongside the existing `ReasonerConfig::complete()`.\n\nTo support this, `ReasonerResult::Inconsistent`/`OwnedReasonerResult::Inconsistent` change from a single `{ reason, witnesses }` pair to `{ reports: Vec<InconsistencyReport> }` / `Vec<OwnedInconsistencyReport>`. Unlike growl's CLI, which collapses to the first report only to preserve prior single-report behavior (see the \"ReasonerResult's inconsistent variant ... carries a list\" Consequence), the Rust API exposes every report even on the plain (non-validate) `reason()` path — favoring API completeness for library consumers over matching the CLI's collapsed UX.\n\nEvidence: rust/README.md diff — new \"### Validation\" section; Quick Start and advanced-usage match examples changing `Inconsistent { reason, witnesses }` to `Inconsistent { reports }` for both `ReasonerResult` and `OwnedReasonerResult`; `ReasonerConfig`'s builder-chain example gaining `.validate(true)`/`.validate_ns(...)`; new `Reasoner::new().complete(true)` example; new `ValidateReport`/`ValidateResult`/`OwnedValidateReport`/`OwnedValidateResult` type blocks and free-function listings. Confirmed still current at HEAD: rust/src/lib.rs:561 (`InconsistencyReport`), :580 (`Inconsistent { reports }`), :650 (`ValidateResult`), :764 (`pub fn validate`), :1343 (`Reasoner::validate`)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d034f76d-5c48-4ee6-9fbe-9a22806f21e0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
