<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d60af8ac-5d68-4eaf-8669-73f5ccf1ed33> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "TBox validation mode via synthetic instance injection" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d60af8ac-5d68-4eaf-8669-73f5ccf1ed33> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/365040dc-aee8-456c-936c-47a7dbb4c79b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d60af8ac-5d68-4eaf-8669-73f5ccf1ed33> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/bfddb2b9-baed-4f0a-a841-6ce6ff4c9dc0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d60af8ac-5d68-4eaf-8669-73f5ccf1ed33> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/e71422b6-0c80-4741-aa68-a27243061168> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d60af8ac-5d68-4eaf-8669-73f5ccf1ed33> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d60af8ac-5d68-4eaf-8669-73f5ccf1ed33> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Growl gains a --validate CLI flag that checks whether an ontology's declared classes and properties are satisfiable: it injects a synthetic blank-node instance for each declared class/property, runs reasoning to fixpoint, and scans for inconsistencies triggered by those synthetic individuals using six existing check rules (cls-nothing2, cax-dw, cax-adc, cls-com, prp-asyp, prp-pdw). Unlike ordinary inconsistency detection (which reports only the first witness), validate mode reports ALL unsatisfiable entities found. A new --validate-ns <prefix> flag scopes which entities get synthetic instances/validation to those whose IRI starts with the given prefix, so validating a domain ontology loaded alongside a large background TLO (via the new --background/-b flag) doesn't also validate every TLO class. --validate overrides --fast (a warning is printed) because validation needs schema materialization; --emit is ignored in validate mode (also warned).\n\nWhy + evidence: commit 390247b3a9 (#15, \"Added validate mode\") adds README.md's \"### Validate Mode\" section documenting the synthetic-injection approach, the six check rules, --validate-ns, and --background; cli/main.slop adds --validate/--validate-ns/--background/-b flag parsing, `validate` and `validate-ns` fields on ReasonerConfig, the \"Warning: --validate overrides --fast\" and \"Warning: --emit is ignored in --validate mode\" print statements, and a validate-mode success/failure branch (\"[PASS] Validation passed\" / \"[FAIL] Validation found N unsatisfiable entities\" listing each report's reason). README's documented `make conformance` test count moves 91 -> 92, consistent with one new conformance test for this feature." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d60af8ac-5d68-4eaf-8669-73f5ccf1ed33> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d60af8ac-5d68-4eaf-8669-73f5ccf1ed33> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-17T06:03:03Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
