<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d71850ff-e985-4682-b019-a69b52c0aa02> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d71850ff-e985-4682-b019-a69b52c0aa02> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Refresh README verification proof counts" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d71850ff-e985-4682-b019-a69b52c0aa02> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/365040dc-aee8-456c-936c-47a7dbb4c79b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d71850ff-e985-4682-b019-a69b52c0aa02> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d71850ff-e985-4682-b019-a69b52c0aa02> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "README.md's \"## Verification\" section enumerated proof counts are updated to reflect grown Z3-verified contract coverage: \"104 function-level contracts are verified\" (was 101); soundness \"Covers 56 of 77 inference functions\" (was 55); completeness now enumerates (eq-sym/trans, prp-symp, scm-cls, scm-eqc1/eqc2, scm-eqc-mutual, scm-eqp1/eqp2, scm-eqp-mutual, scm-op, scm-dp), \"12 functions\" (was eq-sym, scm-eqc1/eqc2, prp-symp, scm-eqp1/eqp2, \"8 functions\"); novelty now enumerates \"cls-maxc2, cls-maxqc3, cls-maxqc4, and transitive-closure\", \"4 functions\" (was those three cardinality functions only, \"3 functions\").\n\nThis surfaces two facts not previously captured in project memory: (1) scm-eqp-mutual (equivalentProperty from mutual subPropertyOf — the property-side analogue of scm-eqc-mutual) gained a completeness contract; (2) a \"transitive-closure\" function gained a novelty contract, alongside the already-recorded cardinality functions cls-maxc2/cls-maxqc3/cls-maxqc4. The remaining count changes (eq-trans's completeness now documented in prose; scm-cls/scm-eqc-mutual/scm-op/scm-dp completeness) match the immediately preceding \"Contract strengthening across scm, cls, eq, and prp rules\" commit (PR #11, merge 6e94c8a2eb, captured minutes earlier), which this commit's README update makes public-facing for the first time.\n\nEvidence: commit eaaab278be12a7ddcf655f4a01bcd243dc332c14 (PR #12 \"README update\") diff on README.md, the three \"## Verification\" bullet points (Soundness/Completeness/Novelty) and the `slop verify` function-count sentence." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d71850ff-e985-4682-b019-a69b52c0aa02> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
