<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d85628f7-2bb7-43d8-807b-98dd50fc77a3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d85628f7-2bb7-43d8-807b-98dd50fc77a3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Batch-construct initial Delta, skip seen-set population" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d85628f7-2bb7-43d8-807b-98dd50fc77a3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/7a377274-e1bc-43a2-b657-8ae3e39fdefb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d85628f7-2bb7-43d8-807b-98dd50fc77a3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d85628f7-2bb7-43d8-807b-98dd50fc77a3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "engine-make-initial-delta (src/engine.slop) now builds its triples list and by-predicate index in a single direct `for-each` pass over `(. g triples)` — appending each triple to a plain list and inserting it into a manually-populated by-predicate `Map Term (Set Triple)` — instead of calling `indexed-graph-for-each` + `delta-add` once per triple as it did before. Critically, the resulting Delta's `seen` set is now built fresh/empty (`(set-new arena Triple)`) rather than populated with every initial triple, because (per the new code comment) \"the initial delta is read-only (rules read from it but produce into new deltas), and graph triples are already deduplicated, so dedup via seen is unnecessary.\"\n\nWhy + evidence: commit cd0f8210dd (#19, \"Improvements for memory usage\") diff on src/engine.slop — engine-make-initial-delta's body changes from `(let ((mut d (make-delta arena 0))) (indexed-graph-for-each g (none) (none) (none) (fn ((t Triple)) (set! d (delta-add arena d t)))) d)` to a `(let ((mut triples-list (list-new arena Triple)) (mut by-pred (map-new arena Term (Set Triple)))) (for-each (t (. g triples)) (list-push triples-list t) (let ((pred (triple-predicate t))) (match (map-get by-pred pred) ((some pred-set) (set-put pred-set t)) ((none) (let ((new-set (set-new arena Triple))) (set-put new-set t) (map-put by-pred pred new-set)))))) (record-new Delta (triples triples-list) (seen (set-new arena Triple)) (by-predicate by-pred) (iteration 0)))` block, with the added comments \"This saves ~1.85 GB for 7.7M triples (no hash set of all triples)\" and \"Note: uses for-each over g.triples (not indexed-graph-for-each) because closures can't capture arena for set-put/map-put operations.\"\n\nThis reverses, at this one call site only, the \"Stream graph matches via indexed-graph-for-each\" decision's earlier choice (commit 75b17fd) to seed this exact function's delta via `indexed-graph-for-each` + `delta-add`: the pre-commit body of engine-make-initial-delta is a verbatim match for that decision's documented \"engine-run-iteration-0's delta seed\" rewrite. The other call sites that decision touched (cax-sco, cax-eqc1/2, cls-int1/2, cls-uni1, cls-svf1, cls-avf1, cls-hv1) are untouched by this commit, so this is a narrow, call-site-specific reversal for memory reasons, not a full retraction of that decision." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d85628f7-2bb7-43d8-807b-98dd50fc77a3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d85628f7-2bb7-43d8-807b-98dd50fc77a3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-04-13T03:04:30Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
