<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d8e27793-5b36-482b-9049-33fd91ae4b8f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d8e27793-5b36-482b-9049-33fd91ae4b8f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Toolchain-free C build for growl" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d8e27793-5b36-482b-9049-33fd91ae4b8f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/74af8f69-d68a-4db6-a495-07bb196e4866> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d8e27793-5b36-482b-9049-33fd91ae4b8f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d8e27793-5b36-482b-9049-33fd91ae4b8f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "growl's CLI and test binaries are now built by a plain Makefile invoking `cc` directly over a checked-in csrc/ tree, instead of requiring the SLOP toolchain (`slop build`/`slop test`) to compile.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit c2c82d6 (\"added C source and Makefile\") adds a root Makefile whose header states \"Growl — OWL 2 RL Reasoner / Build from transpiled C sources — no SLOP toolchain required.\" Its `cli`/`test`/`release` targets compile csrc/src/*.c against csrc/runtime/slop_runtime.h with plain `$(CC) $(CFLAGS)`, with no dependency on `slop`, SLOP_HOME, or slop.toml at build time. The same commit adds csrc/generate_c.py, the separate script that produces/refreshes those C sources from the .slop originals by driving slop's ModuleResolver plus the native `slop-compiler transpile`; that regeneration step still requires SLOP_HOME (to locate the compiler binary and stdlib), but it is decoupled from the day-to-day build/test loop the Makefile drives." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d8e27793-5b36-482b-9049-33fd91ae4b8f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d8e27793-5b36-482b-9049-33fd91ae4b8f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-07T06:16:37Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d8e27793-5b36-482b-9049-33fd91ae4b8f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Toolchain-free C build for growl" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d8e27793-5b36-482b-9049-33fd91ae4b8f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/75e4a450-3cce-42a1-9097-f9216d81e0c9> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d8e27793-5b36-482b-9049-33fd91ae4b8f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/a9670bca-b5b8-4137-b231-505d0643d52f> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d8e27793-5b36-482b-9049-33fd91ae4b8f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/f2130f54-8dba-4e2a-970f-c28fc2e3ba32> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/dde4e458-a6c7-4fd4-9098-3eac60412962> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/dde4e458-a6c7-4fd4-9098-3eac60412962> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Locate slop stdlib via ${SLOP_HOME} env var" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/dde4e458-a6c7-4fd4-9098-3eac60412962> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/9f7a7679-6c17-40b2-bbef-b78d9832bfa1> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/dde4e458-a6c7-4fd4-9098-3eac60412962> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/dde4e458-a6c7-4fd4-9098-3eac60412962> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "slop.toml's [build].include and [test].include are each extended with an entry pointing into an environment-variable-resolved path, \"${SLOP_HOME}/lib/std/\" (build) and \"${SLOP_HOME}/lib/std\" (test) — previously [build].include was [\"../slop-rdf\", \"src\"] and [test].include was [\"../slop-rdf\", \"src\", \"src/rules\"]. This means growl's build and test targets now resolve the slop standard library through a SLOP_HOME-configured toolchain installation, in addition to the sibling slop-rdf checkout already referenced via the relative path \"../slop-rdf\". Evidence: commit 5ef7e90 (\"include fixes\") diff hunks on slop.toml, appending the ${SLOP_HOME}/lib/std path to both the [build] and [test] include lists." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/dde4e458-a6c7-4fd4-9098-3eac60412962> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
