<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ec1a20cc-42ab-4866-8592-cafd6792a677> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ec1a20cc-42ab-4866-8592-cafd6792a677> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Growl gains a --enrich/-e CLI flag (plus ReasonerConfig.enrich and Rust Reasoner::enrich()/ReasonerConfig::enrich()) that runs a targeted subset of OWL 2 RL rules instead of full reasoning: property propagation (prp-dom, prp-rng, prp-spo1/2, prp-eqp1/2, prp-inv1/2, prp-symp, prp-trp), subclass/equivalent-class propagation (cax-sco, cax-eqc1/2), and consistency checks (prp-asyp, prp-irp, prp-pdw, prp-adp, prp-npa1/2, cax-dw, cax-adc) still run, while sameAs generators (prp-fp, prp-ifp, prp-key), all eq-* rules, all cls-* class-expression rules, schema materialization (scm-*), and datatype rules (dt-type1/2, dt-not-type) are skipped.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit b61d7277b1 (#16, \"added enrichment mode\"). README.md's new \"### Enrich Mode\" section states the flag \"materializes a targeted subset of rules ... while skipping sameAs generators, class expressions, and schema materialization\" for \"practical ontology enrichment without the overhead and triple explosion of full OWL reasoning.\" src/engine.slop gates schema-materialize, dt-type1, dt-not-type, eq-ref, and the eq/cls sub-worker spawns behind `(not enrich)` (sequential and parallel paths both); src/rules/prp.slop's apply-prp-rules gains an `enrich` parameter that specifically skips prp-fp/prp-ifp/prp-key because (per its new comment) they \"produce sameAs.\" cli/main.slop adds -e/--enrich, warns when combined with --fast (\"--enrich overrides --fast\") or --complete (\"--enrich and --complete are conflicting; --enrich skips most rules\") rather than erroring, and threads (. args enrich) into the ReasonerConfig. rust/src/lib.rs adds Reasoner::enrich()/ReasonerConfig::enrich(), and Reasoner::reason() now applies both complete and enrich onto the default config. Four new test-cli.slop tests (21-24) assert cax-sco subclass propagation still fires, sameAs transitivity is skipped, cls-hv1 is skipped, and cax-dw disjoint-class detection still fires under --enrich." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ec1a20cc-42ab-4866-8592-cafd6792a677> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ec1a20cc-42ab-4866-8592-cafd6792a677> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-03-01T17:50:49Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
