<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ec1a20cc-42ab-4866-8592-cafd6792a677> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/32dab2aa-60bf-4573-88f8-422d531ac146> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ec1a20cc-42ab-4866-8592-cafd6792a677> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b4e4407f-4089-4538-be61-33a5074d7cf2> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ec1a20cc-42ab-4866-8592-cafd6792a677> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/fc50222b-7d70-4131-837d-ea33d5f6eed6> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f0c5db6f-59bf-4db9-9ff3-a42b61640275> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f0c5db6f-59bf-4db9-9ff3-a42b61640275> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Ordered XSD value comparison added as dormant infrastructure" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f0c5db6f-59bf-4db9-9ff3-a42b61640275> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f0c5db6f-59bf-4db9-9ff3-a42b61640275> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "csrc/src/slop_xsd.c/.h (hand-written C, not generated from a .slop source — there is no src/xsd.slop) gain three new functions in this commit: xsd_float_cmp(a, b) (double comparison to less/equal/greater), xsd_values_compare(XsdValue, XsdValue) (numeric-type-coercing comparison across integer/decimal/float/double, returning `incomparable` for non-numeric or mismatched types), and xsd_compare(arena, Term, Term) (Term-level wrapper). A new xsd_XsdCompareResult enum (less/equal/greater/incomparable) is added alongside, and both are re-exported through include/growl.h with C-interop aliases (xsd_xsd_compare, xsd_xsd_values_compare).\n\nThis is ordering comparison, a capability distinct from and additional to the existing xsd_values_equal/xsd_literal_values_equal equality-only functions. `git grep xsd_compare|xsd_values_compare` across this commit's src/rules/*.slop, src/growl.slop, and src/filter.slop shows no caller anywhere — no rule function, filter, or public API entry point uses it yet. slop_vocab.c/.h also gain two new SHACL term constants in the same commit (vocab_SHACL_LANGUAGE_IN, vocab_SHACL_UNIQUE_LANG), also uncalled elsewhere in this diff. Both additions land in the same merge as the contract-strengthening work (see \"Contract strengthening across scm, cls, eq, and prp rules\") but are functionally unrelated to it and to each other's use site — they read as infrastructure staged ahead of a not-yet-implemented consumer (plausibly future SHACL constraint support or numeric-ordering OWL 2 RL rules), mirroring the earlier \"SLOP_ARENA_NO_CAP build-time arena-cap bypass\" pattern of committing dormant capability before it is wired up." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f0c5db6f-59bf-4db9-9ff3-a42b61640275> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f0c5db6f-59bf-4db9-9ff3-a42b61640275> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-11T07:38:58Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f0c5db6f-59bf-4db9-9ff3-a42b61640275> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Ordered XSD value comparison added as dormant infrastructure" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f3641e03-9d08-42da-8abc-0eaa4e24930e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f3641e03-9d08-42da-8abc-0eaa4e24930e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Reasonable added to benchmark comparison harness" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f3641e03-9d08-42da-8abc-0eaa4e24930e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/e71422b6-0c80-4741-aa68-a27243061168> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f3641e03-9d08-42da-8abc-0eaa4e24930e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f3641e03-9d08-42da-8abc-0eaa4e24930e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "cli/tests/benchmark_compare.py's compare_mode now also runs `reasonable` (a fast Rust-based OWL 2 RL reasoner, via the Python `reasonable` package) alongside the existing OWL-RL ground truth and Growl comparisons, printing a \"Reasonable\" row (input/inferred/total/time) in the comparison table and a \"Growl fast vs Reasonable\" inferred-count diff line.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit d54cf78 (merge PR #7 from Trivyn/dttype2, \"Fixing up rust wrapper\"). benchmark_compare.py's module docstring changes from \"Reasoner comparison: OWL-RL (ground truth) vs Growl\" to \"Reasoner comparison: OWL-RL (ground truth) vs Reasonable vs Growl\", adds \"Reasonable is a fast Rust-based OWL 2 RL reasoner for performance comparison\", and the Requires line changes to \"pip install owlrl rdflib reasonable\". A new run_reasonable(path) function (cli/tests/benchmark_compare.py:67) parses the fixture with rdflib and runs `reasonable.PyReasoner().from_graph(g).reason()` RUNS times taking the median; compare_mode() calls it per-fixture and prints its row plus the new \"Growl fast vs Reasonable\" diff line." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f3641e03-9d08-42da-8abc-0eaa4e24930e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f3641e03-9d08-42da-8abc-0eaa4e24930e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-09T06:09:50Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f3641e03-9d08-42da-8abc-0eaa4e24930e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Reasonable added to benchmark comparison harness" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f369f216-61e5-4e64-ae90-60f12b474c14> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f369f216-61e5-4e64-ae90-60f12b474c14> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Config-driven max-triples cancellation guard" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f369f216-61e5-4e64-ae90-60f12b474c14> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/7a377274-e1bc-43a2-b657-8ae3e39fdefb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f369f216-61e5-4e64-ae90-60f12b474c14> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/833a482a-9217-4511-99e7-1166a8c28fbb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f369f216-61e5-4e64-ae90-60f12b474c14> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/9f7a7679-6c17-40b2-bbef-b78d9832bfa1> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
