<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/fa819b9d-6bdb-483f-aa99-0e6e59058bf8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/a1504e54-ade5-48ea-978e-0d454daa71e6> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/0213903f-546c-416a-a432-312c595b1de2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/0213903f-546c-416a-a432-312c595b1de2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A future build target can bypass the hard-coded SLOP_ARENA_MAX_TOTAL_BYTES ceiling (and its abort()-on-exceeded behavior) by defining SLOP_ARENA_NO_CAP, without editing slop_runtime.h itself; as of this commit no build target does so, so default cap-enforcing behavior is unchanged." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/0213903f-546c-416a-a432-312c595b1de2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
