<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8594f3ad-fe7b-443a-b183-1e0b2dcc5a03> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-07T04:53:15Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8594f3ad-fe7b-443a-b183-1e0b2dcc5a03> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Running growl --quiet is no longer fully silent — it always writes one machine-parseable summary line to stdout for both consistent and inconsistent outcomes, which the new cli/tests/benchmark.sh script depends on to collect parse/reason timings and triple counts across benchmark fixtures." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8a3470de-81d7-469f-8056-88373fca3b1c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8a3470de-81d7-469f-8056-88373fca3b1c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Every C source in growl's csrc/ tree that pattern-matches on the rdf_Term tag (hash/eq helpers, term-kind dispatch, term_free) must now handle a 4th `term_triple` arm or the switch becomes non-exhaustive; this single commit touches slop_cax.c, slop_cls.c, slop_dt.c, slop_engine.c/h, slop_eq.c, slop_filter.h, slop_growl.c, slop_index.c/h, slop_prp.c, slop_rdf.c/h, slop_scm.c, slop_serialize_ttl.c/h, slop_test_cli.c, slop_ttl.c/h, and slop_types.c/h." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8a3470de-81d7-469f-8056-88373fca3b1c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8a3470de-81d7-469f-8056-88373fca3b1c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8a3470de-81d7-469f-8056-88373fca3b1c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-26T02:39:08Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8a3470de-81d7-469f-8056-88373fca3b1c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Every C source in growl's csrc/ tree that pattern-matches on the rdf_Term tag (hash/eq helpers, term-kind dispatch, term_free) must now handle a 4th `term_triple` arm or the switch becomes non-exhaustive; this single commit touches slop_cax.c, slop_cls.c, slop_dt.c, slop_engine.c/h, slop_eq.c, slop_filter.h, slop_growl.c, slop_index.c/h, slop_prp.c, slop_rdf.c/h, slop_scm.c, slop_serialize_ttl.c/h, slop_test_cli.c, slop_ttl.c/h, and slop_types.c/h." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8a3e51d7-690e-437f-b81e-e0d674416c2e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8a3e51d7-690e-437f-b81e-e0d674416c2e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Delta carries an additional Set<Triple> alongside its List<Triple>, trading memory for O(1) dedup checks so delta-add stays tractable when reasoning over real-world-scale ontologies like BFO." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8a3e51d7-690e-437f-b81e-e0d674416c2e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
