<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8a3e51d7-690e-437f-b81e-e0d674416c2e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-03T15:29:45Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8a3e51d7-690e-437f-b81e-e0d674416c2e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Delta carries an additional Set<Triple> alongside its List<Triple>, trading memory for O(1) dedup checks so delta-add stays tractable when reasoning over real-world-scale ontologies like BFO." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8d543d2a-1fde-4552-ad42-542431aae264> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8d543d2a-1fde-4552-ad42-542431aae264> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Reasonable accuracy re-measured after double-count fix" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8d543d2a-1fde-4552-ad42-542431aae264> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/e71422b6-0c80-4741-aa68-a27243061168> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8d543d2a-1fde-4552-ad42-542431aae264> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8d543d2a-1fde-4552-ad42-542431aae264> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "README.md's Accuracy table \"Reasonable\" column is re-measured after fixing benchmark_compare.py's double-counting bug (see Lesson \"Reasonable's reason() returns full closure, not delta\"), giving new percentages relative to OWL-RL ground truth: BFO -75.6%, Pizza -88.3%, CCO -59.9%, Schema.org -15.8%, Brick -29.9% -- replacing the prior (bug-affected) snapshot of BFO -34.3%, Pizza -64.0%, CCO -34.8%, Schema.org +28.7%, Brick +104.2%. The Growl --fast column also shifts (e.g. Brick -69.5%->-47.2%) because --fast now materializes scm-sco/scm-eqc1. With both fixes applied, Growl --fast and Reasonable now track closely (residual differences: BFO -22, Pizza -231, CCO +4,372, Schema.org -3,175, Brick -6,824 inferred triples), with the remaining gap attributed to Reasonable's non-standard universal owl:Thing typing that --fast deliberately does not replicate." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8d543d2a-1fde-4552-ad42-542431aae264> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8d543d2a-1fde-4552-ad42-542431aae264> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/28bdd8f8-ba11-4237-893f-654804a1c8ec> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8d543d2a-1fde-4552-ad42-542431aae264> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-29T18:50:33Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8d543d2a-1fde-4552-ad42-542431aae264> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Reasonable accuracy re-measured after double-count fix" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8d543d2a-1fde-4552-ad42-542431aae264> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6cb7f398-ac5c-43f0-a62c-828025adc7d5> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8d543d2a-1fde-4552-ad42-542431aae264> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/1f9d7ea9-2166-4a18-bf4e-2014b7baebd3> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/95fb64cf-0ba3-4f24-9192-30608b3983b6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/95fb64cf-0ba3-4f24-9192-30608b3983b6> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Large ontologies that would otherwise grow unbounded during reasoning can now be automatically bounded by triple count without the caller having to wire up and poll an external atomic cancel-ptr flag — the max-triples check reuses the same done/cancelled halt mechanism and reason-cancelled partial-result variant that cooperative cancellation introduced." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/95fb64cf-0ba3-4f24-9192-30608b3983b6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/95fb64cf-0ba3-4f24-9192-30608b3983b6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/95fb64cf-0ba3-4f24-9192-30608b3983b6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-04-13T03:04:30Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/95fb64cf-0ba3-4f24-9192-30608b3983b6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Large ontologies that would otherwise grow unbounded during reasoning can now be automatically bounded by triple count without the caller having to wire up and poll an external atomic cancel-ptr flag — the max-triples check reuses the same done/cancelled halt mechanism and reason-cancelled partial-result variant that cooperative cancellation introduced." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/9c583e55-2542-4b46-8e6d-112ab87ad576> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/9c583e55-2542-4b46-8e6d-112ab87ad576> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Releasing growl for a new platform (or compiler) requires adding a new matrix entry to release.yml, not just a local Makefile change — the release surface (linux-x86_64, macos-arm64) is now fixed by the CI matrix rather than whatever the releaser happens to build locally." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/9c583e55-2542-4b46-8e6d-112ab87ad576> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/9c583e55-2542-4b46-8e6d-112ab87ad576> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/9c583e55-2542-4b46-8e6d-112ab87ad576> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-09T18:52:51Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/9c583e55-2542-4b46-8e6d-112ab87ad576> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Releasing growl for a new platform (or compiler) requires adding a new matrix entry to release.yml, not just a local Makefile change — the release surface (linux-x86_64, macos-arm64) is now fixed by the CI matrix rather than whatever the releaser happens to build locally." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/9c639dae-adf9-438c-90d9-ca3e4eeeeebc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/9c639dae-adf9-438c-90d9-ca3e4eeeeebc> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rust integration tests no longer take a static C_LOCK Mutex before each test and rust/README.md's documented test command changes from `cargo test -- --test-threads=1` to plain `cargo test`, since the intern pool is now internally synchronized" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/9c639dae-adf9-438c-90d9-ca3e4eeeeebc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/9c639dae-adf9-438c-90d9-ca3e4eeeeebc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/9c639dae-adf9-438c-90d9-ca3e4eeeeebc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-09T07:10:05Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/9c639dae-adf9-438c-90d9-ca3e4eeeeebc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rust integration tests no longer take a static C_LOCK Mutex before each test and rust/README.md's documented test command changes from `cargo test -- --test-threads=1` to plain `cargo test`, since the intern pool is now internally synchronized" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/a1504e54-ade5-48ea-978e-0d454daa71e6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/a1504e54-ade5-48ea-978e-0d454daa71e6> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rust builds recompile all of growl's vendored C sources via build.rs on every `cargo build`/`cargo test` rather than linking a prebuilt libgrowl.a, consistent with growl's existing toolchain-free C build for CLI/test/release — Rust consumers never need the SLOP toolchain installed." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/a1504e54-ade5-48ea-978e-0d454daa71e6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/a1504e54-ade5-48ea-978e-0d454daa71e6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/a1504e54-ade5-48ea-978e-0d454daa71e6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-09T00:26:48Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/a1504e54-ade5-48ea-978e-0d454daa71e6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rust builds recompile all of growl's vendored C sources via build.rs on every `cargo build`/`cargo test` rather than linking a prebuilt libgrowl.a, consistent with growl's existing toolchain-free C build for CLI/test/release — Rust consumers never need the SLOP toolchain installed." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/a23f9fc4-7a6c-41b2-aa31-997f66d5faf0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/a23f9fc4-7a6c-41b2-aa31-997f66d5faf0> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Every IndexedGraph insertion (rdf_indexed_graph_add) now does one additional nested-map upsert (into pos) per triple, alongside the existing spo/pso/osp upserts -- a small constant-factor increase in insert-time work and memory traded for the query-time win." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/a23f9fc4-7a6c-41b2-aa31-997f66d5faf0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
