<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/c5645040-9d1a-4f49-9ab8-8dec864a4c32> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-07T07:36:12Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/c5645040-9d1a-4f49-9ab8-8dec864a4c32> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Fast mode trades OWL 2 RL soundness/completeness for speed: schema closure (scm-*) and several consistency/cardinality checks are not derived or enforced when --fast is set, so results may differ from full-profile reasoning on ontologies that rely on inferred (rather than explicit) subClassOf/subPropertyOf chains, or that would otherwise trigger the skipped disjointness/functional-property/cardinality violations." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/c698fa83-bb8f-4c9f-a344-37afcbc342a4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/c698fa83-bb8f-4c9f-a344-37afcbc342a4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Growl --fast is faster than Reasonable on all five benchmarked ontologies for the first time -- previously (per the pre-commit README) it was slower on Schema.org (333ms vs 132ms) and Brick (2.3s vs 286ms); post-commit it leads on all five (e.g. Brick 98ms vs 204ms), matching the new README claim 'At equivalent rule coverage, Growl --fast is faster than Reasonable on all five ontologies.'" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/c698fa83-bb8f-4c9f-a344-37afcbc342a4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
