<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/c698fa83-bb8f-4c9f-a344-37afcbc342a4> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Growl --fast is faster than Reasonable on all five benchmarked ontologies for the first time -- previously (per the pre-commit README) it was slower on Schema.org (333ms vs 132ms) and Brick (2.3s vs 286ms); post-commit it leads on all five (e.g. Brick 98ms vs 204ms), matching the new README claim 'At equivalent rule coverage, Growl --fast is faster than Reasonable on all five ontologies.'" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/c78fa5a3-2f0d-414c-8234-90dc258dcba9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/c78fa5a3-2f0d-414c-8234-90dc258dcba9> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Bound-predicate+bound-object-with-unbound-subject IndexedGraph lookups (the pattern rdf:type-membership-propagation rules like cax-sco/cax-eqc1/2 issue) resolve via one O(1) pos[p][o] hash lookup instead of an O(subjects-under-that-predicate) scan through pso testing object-set membership per subject." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
