<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/efa7d6e1-0a5a-4aac-8233-3a5bafbff676> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-17T20:57:19Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/efa7d6e1-0a5a-4aac-8233-3a5bafbff676> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rust library consumers must handle a Vec of InconsistencyReport even for ordinary (non-validate) reason() calls, unlike the CLI's single-report output" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f30fae6c-a26b-4133-ae91-2df8acc648b7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f30fae6c-a26b-4133-ae91-2df8acc648b7> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "25 @loop-invariant blocks across cax.slop, cls.slop, eq.slop, prp.slop, and scm.slop -- including the outer-loop invariants on cax-sco, cax-eqc1, cax-eqc2 and on eq-trans that the 'Loop-invariant proof obligations extended to soundness across rule modules' and 'eq-trans completeness invariant' Constraints established -- were deleted along with the loop restructuring and not restated against the new match-lookup form, so Z3-verified soundness/completeness coverage for those rules is reduced again, extending the same trade-off already accepted once for indexed-graph-for-each callback sites." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f30fae6c-a26b-4133-ae91-2df8acc648b7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f30fae6c-a26b-4133-ae91-2df8acc648b7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f30fae6c-a26b-4133-ae91-2df8acc648b7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-06T18:09:05Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f30fae6c-a26b-4133-ae91-2df8acc648b7> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "25 @loop-invariant blocks across cax.slop, cls.slop, eq.slop, prp.slop, and scm.slop -- including the outer-loop invariants on cax-sco, cax-eqc1, cax-eqc2 and on eq-trans that the 'Loop-invariant proof obligations extended to soundness across rule modules' and 'eq-trans completeness invariant' Constraints established -- were deleted along with the loop restructuring and not restated against the new match-lookup form, so Z3-verified soundness/completeness coverage for those rules is reduced again, extending the same trade-off already accepted once for indexed-graph-for-each callback sites." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f5aec818-ea00-4ffe-b604-b2c557563016> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f5aec818-ea00-4ffe-b604-b2c557563016> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "dt-eq/dt-diff exclusion matches OWL-RL reference behavior" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f5aec818-ea00-4ffe-b604-b2c557563016> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f5aec818-ea00-4ffe-b604-b2c557563016> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Ontologies relying on dt-type2 (literal typing), dt-eq, or dt-diff entailments still see incomplete results from growl. This deliberately matches OWL-RL's (the owlrl reference package's) own choice to skip dt-eq/dt-diff, keeping growl's --complete output comparable to the OWL-RL ground truth used by benchmark_compare.py rather than diverging from it." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f5aec818-ea00-4ffe-b604-b2c557563016> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f5aec818-ea00-4ffe-b604-b2c557563016> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-08T06:51:50Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f5aec818-ea00-4ffe-b604-b2c557563016> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "dt-eq/dt-diff exclusion matches OWL-RL reference behavior" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f5aec818-ea00-4ffe-b604-b2c557563016> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/936b0242-4d2d-4a63-ab18-cc1487241b43> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f6078a18-1eb7-4114-a27a-ebbe637e23df> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f6078a18-1eb7-4114-a27a-ebbe637e23df> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Converting an IndexedGraph to a Graph for --emit serialization or test assertions no longer copies each triple through an arena-allocated for-each/graph-add loop — it reuses IndexedGraph's existing triples list by reference and casts indexed-graph-size to GraphSize directly, avoiding an O(n) copy that would otherwise scale with graph size (relevant given this same commit adds Brick.ttl (48827 lines) and schemaorg.ttl (21562 lines) as benchmark fixtures)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f6078a18-1eb7-4114-a27a-ebbe637e23df> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f6078a18-1eb7-4114-a27a-ebbe637e23df> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f6078a18-1eb7-4114-a27a-ebbe637e23df> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-07T04:53:15Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f6078a18-1eb7-4114-a27a-ebbe637e23df> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Converting an IndexedGraph to a Graph for --emit serialization or test assertions no longer copies each triple through an arena-allocated for-each/graph-add loop — it reuses IndexedGraph's existing triples list by reference and casts indexed-graph-size to GraphSize directly, avoiding an O(n) copy that would otherwise scale with graph size (relevant given this same commit adds Brick.ttl (48827 lines) and schemaorg.ttl (21562 lines) as benchmark fixtures)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f8a6ccb3-0b97-4bbf-877b-a66c13f20506> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f8a6ccb3-0b97-4bbf-877b-a66c13f20506> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ReasonerResult's inconsistent variant (reason-inconsistent) now carries a list of InconsistencyReport instead of a single report, so validate mode can enumerate every unsatisfiable entity; the non-validate path extracts just the first element (list-get reports 0) to preserve prior single-report CLI behavior, per cli/main.slop's `(match (list-get reports 0) ...)` branch." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f8a6ccb3-0b97-4bbf-877b-a66c13f20506> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f8a6ccb3-0b97-4bbf-877b-a66c13f20506> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f8a6ccb3-0b97-4bbf-877b-a66c13f20506> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-17T06:03:03Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f8a6ccb3-0b97-4bbf-877b-a66c13f20506> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "ReasonerResult's inconsistent variant (reason-inconsistent) now carries a list of InconsistencyReport instead of a single report, so validate mode can enumerate every unsatisfiable entity; the non-validate path extracts just the first element (list-get reports 0) to preserve prior single-report CLI behavior, per cli/main.slop's `(match (list-get reports 0) ...)` branch." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f8d8232d-3f13-41ed-aeb9-63de70400651> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Consequence> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f8d8232d-3f13-41ed-aeb9-63de70400651> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Reasonable's own accuracy vs OWL-RL published, showing wide divergence" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f8d8232d-3f13-41ed-aeb9-63de70400651> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/e71422b6-0c80-4741-aa68-a27243061168> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f8d8232d-3f13-41ed-aeb9-63de70400651> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f8d8232d-3f13-41ed-aeb9-63de70400651> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "README.md's Accuracy table gains a \"Reasonable\" column reporting Reasonable's inferred-triple-count delta vs the OWL-RL ground truth for the first time (the Performance table already carried a Reasonable timing column from earlier work, but Accuracy did not): BFO +91.9%, Pizza +29.1%, CCO -11.4%, Schema.org +15.9%, Brick +81.9% — a much wider and more inconsistent spread than Growl (non-fast: -17.1%/-30.6%/-1.8%/-0.6%/-23.9%) or Growl --complete (within -1.9%..+2.7% on all five). Reasonable over-infers substantially relative to OWL-RL on 4 of 5 ontologies and under-infers on the fifth (CCO), rather than tracking OWL-RL closely.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit b7236f0645 (\"bench table update\") diff on README.md — the Accuracy table header changes from \"| Ontology | OWL-RL (ref) | Growl --complete | Growl | Growl --fast |\" to insert a new \"Reasonable\" column with the percentages above. The immediately following (unchanged in this diff) \"Modes\" paragraph still frames \"Growl --fast vs Reasonable\" as \"apples-to-apples,\" but that claim is scoped to targeted rule *coverage* (matching Reasonable's skip list, per \"Fast mode runs most consistency checks\") — this new data shows it is not an apples-to-apples match on actual inference-count fidelity to OWL-RL, since Reasonable itself diverges far more from the ground truth than Growl does." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/f8d8232d-3f13-41ed-aeb9-63de70400651> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
