<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/13610b21-6950-4164-85fe-607a21c9bc26> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Constraint> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/13610b21-6950-4164-85fe-607a21c9bc26> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Property contracts extended to cls, dt, eq, and scm rules" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/13610b21-6950-4164-85fe-607a21c9bc26> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4c63dce6-c21e-49fc-a5e1-0d64b5a9c005> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/13610b21-6950-4164-85fe-607a21c9bc26> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8fef3fb8-4281-4f7a-90f3-66558fd98861> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/13610b21-6950-4164-85fe-607a21c9bc26> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/365040dc-aee8-456c-936c-47a7dbb4c79b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/13610b21-6950-4164-85fe-607a21c9bc26> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/13610b21-6950-4164-85fe-607a21c9bc26> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Sixteen previously @property-free OWL 2 RL rule functions gain an explicit (@property soundness ...) contract — cls-int1, cls-int2, cls-uni, cls-svf1, cls-svf2, cls-avf, cls-oo (src/rules/cls.slop), dt-type1 (src/rules/dt.slop), eq-sym, eq-rep-s, eq-rep-p, eq-rep-o (src/rules/eq.slop), and scm-svf1, scm-svf2, scm-avf1, scm-avf2, scm-hv (src/rules/scm.slop) — each proving every output triple is justified by a delta triple. Three cardinality functions (cls-maxc2, cls-maxqc3, cls-maxqc4) gain a (@property novelty ...) contract proving every output triple is new (not already in the graph), since as callback functions over the full graph rather than delta iterators they can't be given the standard soundness shape. Several of the newly-soundness-contracted functions (cls-int1, cls-int2, cls-uni, cls-svf1, cls-avf, eq-sym, eq-rep-s/p/o) are exactly the functions the \"Predicate-indexed Delta lookup for rule matching\" decision rewrote to use by-predicate map lookups, whose per-loop @loop-invariant soundness blocks that rewrite deleted without restatement — this commit re-establishes machine-checked soundness for those functions via a single top-level @property forall/exists over $result and delta.triples instead of restoring per-loop invariants. README.md's rewritten Verification section reports the resulting totals: 55 of 77 inference functions carry a soundness property, 8 carry completeness, 3 carry novelty. Evidence: commit 535cc1e (PR #5 \"more_contracts\", \"More contracts\") diff hunks adding (@property soundness ...)/(@property novelty ...) blocks in src/rules/cls.slop, src/rules/dt.slop, src/rules/eq.slop, src/rules/scm.slop; README.md's Verification section rewrite." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/13610b21-6950-4164-85fe-607a21c9bc26> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
