<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/1e67a29a-4e22-479f-9623-e85e77dbb892> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/365040dc-aee8-456c-936c-47a7dbb4c79b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/1e67a29a-4e22-479f-9623-e85e77dbb892> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/1e67a29a-4e22-479f-9623-e85e77dbb892> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "For cax-sco, cax-eqc1, cax-eqc2, and cls-hv1, the per-loop @loop-invariant soundness contracts the prior constraint recorded no longer exist in source — their governing for-each loops were replaced by indexed-graph-for-each callbacks carrying no invariant annotation. cls-hv2, prp-dom, and prp-rng are not evidenced as changed by this commit and should still be treated as governed by the original loop-invariant discipline until checked in a later episode." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/1e67a29a-4e22-479f-9623-e85e77dbb892> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "proposed" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/1e67a29a-4e22-479f-9623-e85e77dbb892> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e6e3fb80-6b6d-4d93-8751-8835b8e1fbdc> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/1e67a29a-4e22-479f-9623-e85e77dbb892> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-04T23:49:15Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/1e67a29a-4e22-479f-9623-e85e77dbb892> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Loop-invariant soundness proofs dropped for memory-heavy rule functions" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/1e67a29a-4e22-479f-9623-e85e77dbb892> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/f286a5c4-2fe9-44fc-86bc-e986fbd94444> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/49a65175-ddca-419e-9a33-dd3a3fe3b5d9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Constraint> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/49a65175-ddca-419e-9a33-dd3a3fe3b5d9> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "No vendoring of slop-std-sys/slop-rdf-sys shared modules" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/49a65175-ddca-419e-9a33-dd3a3fe3b5d9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/833a482a-9217-4511-99e7-1166a8c28fbb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/49a65175-ddca-419e-9a33-dd3a3fe3b5d9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/49a65175-ddca-419e-9a33-dd3a3fe3b5d9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The Rust crate (rust/csrc/) must not vendor its own copy of the C modules now provided by the slop-std-sys / slop-rdf-sys crates (common, file, index, list, rdf, serialize_ttl, strlib, thread, ttl, vocab, xsd) — consumers that link both the growl crate and slop-std-sys/slop-rdf-sys directly would collide on duplicate C symbols.\n\nEvidence: commit c9a80f902b's Makefile diff adds `SHARED_MODULES := common file index list rdf serialize_ttl strlib thread ttl vocab xsd` with the comment \"These modules are provided by slop-std-sys / slop-rdf-sys from slop-sys v0.2.1. The Rust crate must not vendor its own copy, or consumers linking both copies will collide on duplicate symbols,\" and filters them out of `crate-vendor`'s copied sources/headers (CRATE_SRCS/CRATE_HDRS) plus removes any stale copies already in rust/csrc/src/ before copying." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/49a65175-ddca-419e-9a33-dd3a3fe3b5d9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/49a65175-ddca-419e-9a33-dd3a3fe3b5d9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-10T18:10:28Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/49a65175-ddca-419e-9a33-dd3a3fe3b5d9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "No vendoring of slop-std-sys/slop-rdf-sys shared modules" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/4ae877b4-6766-4663-87dd-91ba8210e76b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Constraint> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/4ae877b4-6766-4663-87dd-91ba8210e76b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fixpoint loop iteration bound invariant" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/4ae877b4-6766-4663-87dd-91ba8210e76b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3f5e5977-57b0-45a1-8b9a-e544cedfd4ce> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/4ae877b4-6766-4663-87dd-91ba8210e76b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8afd2e38-3664-402e-9dbd-30a634c91dc3> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/4ae877b4-6766-4663-87dd-91ba8210e76b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f369f216-61e5-4e64-ae90-60f12b474c14> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/4ae877b4-6766-4663-87dd-91ba8210e76b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/7a377274-e1bc-43a2-b657-8ae3e39fdefb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/4ae877b4-6766-4663-87dd-91ba8210e76b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/4ae877b4-6766-4663-87dd-91ba8210e76b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The main fixpoint while-loop in engine.slop's engine-run now carries an explicit (@loop-invariant {(. state iteration) <= (. config max-iterations)}) annotation, formalizing that the loop counter never exceeds config.max-iterations at any point during iteration — needed for the Z3 verifier to discharge the loop's bound obligation. This machine-checks the bound the \"Semi-naive delta-based fixpoint evaluation\" decision already described informally (\"terminates ... when config.max-iterations is reached\"). Evidence: commit 2bd3333 (subject \"verifies!\") diff hunk adding the @loop-invariant line directly under engine.slop's `(while (and (not done) (< (. state iteration) (. config max-iterations))) ...)`. The same commit also adds indexed-graph-match to engine.slop's import list from the index module, alongside this invariant, as part of getting the module to verify." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/4ae877b4-6766-4663-87dd-91ba8210e76b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/4ae877b4-6766-4663-87dd-91ba8210e76b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-01-27T07:29:22Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/4ae877b4-6766-4663-87dd-91ba8210e76b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Fixpoint loop iteration bound invariant" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/5e1a1737-6252-423e-990a-2a3821076f29> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Constraint> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/5e1a1737-6252-423e-990a-2a3821076f29> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rust Arena must stay !Send + !Sync" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/5e1a1737-6252-423e-990a-2a3821076f29> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b5c132c4-4584-44fe-b2cc-a9d58c885b7d> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/5e1a1737-6252-423e-990a-2a3821076f29> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/833a482a-9217-4511-99e7-1166a8c28fbb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/5e1a1737-6252-423e-990a-2a3821076f29> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/5e1a1737-6252-423e-990a-2a3821076f29> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Growl's C runtime uses a global intern pool (slop_global_intern_pool) that is not thread-safe, so the Rust Arena wrapper must remain !Send + !Sync to prevent callers from using it across threads without external synchronization; multi-threaded callers (e.g. tests) must serialize access with a Mutex around arena creation and use. Evidence: rust/README.md \"Thread Safety\" section (\"The C runtime uses a global intern pool ... that is not thread-safe. The Arena type is !Send + !Sync to prevent accidental cross-thread usage\" + documented Mutex-guarded workaround); rust/src/lib.rs's Arena struct comment (\"*mut SlopArena is already !Send + !Sync because raw pointers don't implement Send/Sync. This is the desired behavior since the C arena is not thread-safe from the caller side.\")." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/5e1a1737-6252-423e-990a-2a3821076f29> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/5e1a1737-6252-423e-990a-2a3821076f29> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-09T00:26:48Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
