<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/bebfc6a4-c3f1-480e-aedd-ec3e6bf64658> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/bebfc6a4-c3f1-480e-aedd-ec3e6bf64658> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "eq-trans (src/rules/eq.slop, OWL 2 RL Table 4 sameAs transitivity rule) now carries an explicit (@property completeness ...) contract stating that every triple in `result` is justified by some delta same-as triple `dt` together with an existing graph same-as edge connecting the other endpoint — plus three matching (@loop-invariant ...) blocks (same predicate, restated per-loop) attached to the outer for-each over `(. delta triples)` and the two inner for-each loops over `y-objects` and `x-subjects`, so the invariant is shown to hold incrementally at every loop step rather than only as a post-hoc @post. This is needed for the Z3 verifier to discharge a completeness obligation for the rule (previously eq-trans only had soundness-style @pre/@post), and is the first use of @loop-invariant inside a rule module's own accumulation loops — the only prior @loop-invariant in the codebase (the \"Fixpoint loop iteration bound invariant\" Constraint) bounds engine.slop's top-level fixpoint iteration count, not a rule's internal derivation logic. The same commit also doubles slop.toml's [verify] timeout from 5000ms to 10000ms, plausibly to give the Z3 solver enough time to discharge these added proof obligations. Evidence: commit fdf140e (\"working on rules\") diff hunks on src/rules/eq.slop (the @property block directly after eq-trans's existing @pre/@post pair, plus three near-identical @loop-invariant blocks under the delta/y-objects/x-subjects for-each loops) and slop.toml (`timeout = 5000` → `timeout = 10000` in [verify])." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/bebfc6a4-c3f1-480e-aedd-ec3e6bf64658> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
