<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/f286a5c4-2fe9-44fc-86bc-e986fbd94444> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/f286a5c4-2fe9-44fc-86bc-e986fbd94444> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "cax-sco, cax-eqc1, cax-eqc2 (src/rules/cax.slop), cls-hv1, cls-hv2 (src/rules/cls.slop), and prp-dom, prp-rng (src/rules/prp.slop) each gain an explicit (@property soundness ...) contract plus matching (@loop-invariant ...) blocks restated at every nested for-each level, extending the per-loop invariant discipline previously used only for eq-trans's completeness proof (see \"eq-trans completeness invariant\") to soundness-style obligations across three more rule modules for the first time. In the same commit, eq.slop's eq-sym function has its informal \"Symmetry property: if we infer (y sameAs x), there must be (x sameAs y) in g\" code comment replaced with an explicit (@property completeness ...) contract plus a matching per-loop @loop-invariant, formalizing what was previously only a comment. The same commit also cuts slop.toml's [verify] timeout from 10000ms back down to 5000ms — reverting the prior commit's doubling — even though this commit adds substantially more proof obligations for the Z3 verifier to discharge across cax/cls/eq/prp. Evidence: commit 283c97e (\"more contract\") diff hunks adding @property/@loop-invariant blocks to src/rules/cax.slop (cax-sco both propagation directions, cax-eqc1, cax-eqc2), src/rules/cls.slop (cls-hv1, cls-hv2), src/rules/eq.slop (eq-sym), src/rules/prp.slop (prp-dom, prp-rng); and slop.toml's [verify] section, `timeout = 10000` → `timeout = 5000`." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/f286a5c4-2fe9-44fc-86bc-e986fbd94444> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
