<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/f351d29d-0bc5-4386-a6fa-2b23b63300db> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Constraint> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/f351d29d-0bc5-4386-a6fa-2b23b63300db> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Contract strengthening across scm, cls, eq, and prp rules" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/f351d29d-0bc5-4386-a6fa-2b23b63300db> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4c63dce6-c21e-49fc-a5e1-0d64b5a9c005> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/f351d29d-0bc5-4386-a6fa-2b23b63300db> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/64832702-061c-4f59-bc38-c41938f8f781> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/f351d29d-0bc5-4386-a6fa-2b23b63300db> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8fef3fb8-4281-4f7a-90f3-66558fd98861> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/f351d29d-0bc5-4386-a6fa-2b23b63300db> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/365040dc-aee8-456c-936c-47a7dbb4c79b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/f351d29d-0bc5-4386-a6fa-2b23b63300db> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/f351d29d-0bc5-4386-a6fa-2b23b63300db> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "PR #11 \"strengthen_contracts\" (merge 6e94c8a2eb) both extends Z3-verifiable contract coverage to previously-uncontracted OWL 2 RL rule functions and tightens the precision of several already-contracted ones' soundness formulas.\n\nFirst-time (@property soundness ...) contracts, where before there was only a no-op `(@post {(list-len $result) >= 0})`: scm-cls (src/rules/scm.slop, reflexive subClassOf/subClassOf-owl:Thing/owl:Nothing-subClassOf/reflexive-equivalentClass), scm-eqc-mutual (equivalentClass from mutual subClassOf), scm-op (reflexive subPropertyOf for object properties), scm-dp (reflexive subPropertyOf for datatype properties) — each also gains one or more (@property completeness-* ...) contracts (e.g. completeness-reflexive/-thing/-nothing/-equiv on scm-cls; completeness-subprop/-equiv on scm-op and scm-dp), the first completeness contracts in scm.slop. cls-thing and cls-nothing1 (axiomatic owl:Thing/owl:Nothing type assertions) and prp-ap (annotation-property type assertions) also gain first-time soundness contracts.\n\nExisting soundness formulas are strengthened with more precise delta-sourcing logic: cls-svf1/cls-svf2 (someValuesFrom) now require the restriction's owl:onProperty to match the triggering delta triple's predicate, not just a bare subject/class match; cls-oo (oneOf) now requires the delta triple's predicate to actually be owl:oneOf (previously missing, so the property was checkable against unrelated delta triples); eq-rep-s/eq-rep-p/eq-rep-o (sameAs-based subject/predicate/object replacement) go from a bare \"some delta triple has predicate sameAs\" claim to a two-path disjunction that ties the specific replaced triple back to both a graph triple and the sameAs edge; eq-ref (reflexive sameAs) goes from a bare subject=object claim to one also requiring delta-sourcing and predicate=sameAs; prp-key (hasKey) goes from a bare predicate=sameAs claim to one requiring x and y share a delta/graph-sourced rdf:type. prp-spo2 (property chain axioms)'s soundness property is corrected from a self-referential, likely-vacuous claim (\"predicate has a chain-axiom to itself\") to an honest, narrower claim that every inferred triple is new — with a comment acknowledging full variable-length chain-path validation is \"beyond annotation\" for now. prp-pdw's witness-count postcondition (added by an earlier commit, see \"Inconsistency report witness-count postconditions\") is raised from >=2 to >=3.\n\nConsequence: slop.toml's [verify] timeout is raised from 25000ms to 120000ms (~4.8x), plausibly to give Z3 enough time to discharge the larger set of proof obligations added here -- continuing the same timeout-tuning pattern as the earlier \"eq-trans completeness invariant\" and \"Loop-invariant proof obligations extended to soundness across rule modules\" commits.\n\nEvidence: `git diff cf8aaf7 7fd8d1e -- src/rules/{cls,eq,prp,scm}.slop` and slop.toml's [verify].timeout hunk. This extends the same discipline as the prior \"Property contracts extended to cls, dt, eq, and scm rules\" and \"Loop-invariant proof obligations extended to soundness across rule modules\" Constraints, without retiring either — those functions still carry contracts; this commit both widens coverage and sharpens precision." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/f351d29d-0bc5-4386-a6fa-2b23b63300db> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/f351d29d-0bc5-4386-a6fa-2b23b63300db> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-11T07:38:58Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/f351d29d-0bc5-4386-a6fa-2b23b63300db> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Contract strengthening across scm, cls, eq, and prp rules" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/0f5b194e-5deb-4565-8724-f188748ceb47> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/0f5b194e-5deb-4565-8724-f188748ceb47> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Hand-written Rust FFI struct mirrors silently drift from the C ABI" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/0f5b194e-5deb-4565-8724-f188748ceb47> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/833a482a-9217-4511-99e7-1166a8c28fbb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/0f5b194e-5deb-4565-8724-f188748ceb47> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/0f5b194e-5deb-4565-8724-f188748ceb47> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "A hand-written #[repr(C)] Rust struct that mirrors a C struct can silently go out of sync with the real C ABI when the C side changes, with no compiler error — the Rust struct still compiles, it just reads fields at the wrong offset. This caused the growl 0.6.0 regression: \"Update slop-rdf for indexing and parsing performance\" added a 4th index field (`pos`) to `index_TripleIndex` in the vendored C, growing `index_IndexedGraph` by 8 bytes, but rust/src/ffi.rs's `TripleIndex` mirror was never updated to add the matching `pos` field — so every field read after the embedded TripleIndex in IndexedGraphFfi (notably `.size`) landed 8 bytes off, and `graph.size()` returned a garbage pointer read from ReasonerSuccessFfi.iterations was likewise corrupted.\n\nEvidence: commit ef9ac8a9eb (\"ABI fix\") adds `pub pos: *mut c_void` to rust/src/ffi.rs's `TripleIndex` with the comment \"4th index added in slop-rdf (growl 0.6.0, ...): a missing field here shifts IndexedGraphFfi.size ... to the wrong offset ... so graph.size() returns a garbage pointer\"; Cargo.toml/slop.toml bump 0.6.0 -> 0.6.1 to ship the fix." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/0f5b194e-5deb-4565-8724-f188748ceb47> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/0f5b194e-5deb-4565-8724-f188748ceb47> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-29T22:51:53Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/0f5b194e-5deb-4565-8724-f188748ceb47> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Hand-written Rust FFI struct mirrors silently drift from the C ABI" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/0f5b194e-5deb-4565-8724-f188748ceb47> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7b7344a7-2437-4975-a59e-7c963dc91b03> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/16cbcbf0-6826-4924-82eb-3ccb5a5fe4fd> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/16cbcbf0-6826-4924-82eb-3ccb5a5fe4fd> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Static inline arena functions need a linkable C shim for Rust FFI" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/16cbcbf0-6826-4924-82eb-3ccb5a5fe4fd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/833a482a-9217-4511-99e7-1166a8c28fbb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/16cbcbf0-6826-4924-82eb-3ccb5a5fe4fd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/16cbcbf0-6826-4924-82eb-3ccb5a5fe4fd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "slop_arena_new/slop_arena_free/slop_intern_string are declared `static inline` in slop_runtime.h, so they have no exported symbol and Rust's `extern \"C\"` bindings cannot link to them directly. A new rust/csrc_shim.c wraps them in real, non-inline functions (growl_arena_new, growl_arena_free, growl_intern_string) with genuine linkage, and rust/build.rs compiles this shim alongside the vendored csrc/src sources so rust/src/ffi.rs's extern \"C\" declarations resolve. Evidence: rust/csrc_shim.c's header comment (\"Thin C shim for static inline arena functions from slop_runtime.h. These are static inline in the header, so they have no exported symbol. We wrap them here so Rust can link to them.\") and its three wrapper functions; rust/build.rs's `build.file(\"csrc_shim.c\")`." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/16cbcbf0-6826-4924-82eb-3ccb5a5fe4fd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/16cbcbf0-6826-4924-82eb-3ccb5a5fe4fd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-09T00:26:48Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/16cbcbf0-6826-4924-82eb-3ccb5a5fe4fd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Static inline arena functions need a linkable C shim for Rust FFI" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/16cbcbf0-6826-4924-82eb-3ccb5a5fe4fd> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/fa819b9d-6bdb-483f-aa99-0e6e59058bf8> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/237b7ca0-7ed3-40b8-8ea9-1c50ae2a731e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/237b7ca0-7ed3-40b8-8ea9-1c50ae2a731e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Background ontology blank nodes need remapping before merge" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/237b7ca0-7ed3-40b8-8ea9-1c50ae2a731e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/9f7a7679-6c17-40b2-bbef-b78d9832bfa1> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/237b7ca0-7ed3-40b8-8ea9-1c50ae2a731e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/e71422b6-0c80-4741-aa68-a27243061168> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/237b7ca0-7ed3-40b8-8ea9-1c50ae2a731e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/237b7ca0-7ed3-40b8-8ea9-1c50ae2a731e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "When --validate merges a --background ontology file's triples into the main graph for combined reasoning, the background file's blank node IDs must be remapped by an offset (max-blank-id-in-graph(main-graph) + 1, via a new remap-blank-term helper) before the merge — otherwise the background file's independently-parsed, independently-numbered blank nodes collide with the main file's blank node IDs, silently conflating distinct anonymous individuals from the two files. cli/main.slop's background-merge block computes bg-blank-offset and calls remap-blank-term on every background triple's subject and object before adding it to the combined indexed graph.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit 390247b3a9's PR body lists \"validation fix for bnode name collisions\" as a distinct fix commit within the PR (#15, \"Added validate mode\"); growl's public API gains new exported `remap-blank-term` and `max-blank-id-in-graph` functions (imported into cli/main.slop's growl import list) used specifically in the background-merge path, not in the plain single-file path." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/237b7ca0-7ed3-40b8-8ea9-1c50ae2a731e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/237b7ca0-7ed3-40b8-8ea9-1c50ae2a731e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-17T06:03:03Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/237b7ca0-7ed3-40b8-8ea9-1c50ae2a731e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Background ontology blank nodes need remapping before merge" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/237b7ca0-7ed3-40b8-8ea9-1c50ae2a731e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d60af8ac-5d68-4eaf-8669-73f5ccf1ed33> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/2c302389-f358-4a27-b3a8-32852c704855> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/2c302389-f358-4a27-b3a8-32852c704855> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Delta-based rule tests must trigger via the Delta, not the Graph" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/2c302389-f358-4a27-b3a8-32852c704855> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/365040dc-aee8-456c-936c-47a7dbb4c79b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/2c302389-f358-4a27-b3a8-32852c704855> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/2c302389-f358-4a27-b3a8-32852c704855> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "In growl's semi-naive delta-based fixpoint engine, rule modules evaluate each iteration against the current Delta, not a full re-scan of the accumulated Graph — so a rule-module @example whose triggering triple lives only in the initial Graph fixture (paired with fixture-delta-empty) never actually exercises the rule under test. Commit 7b74989 (\"fix the growl tests!\") fixes this across cax.slop, eq.slop, prp.slop, and scm.slop by moving each rule-triggering triple out of the graph fixture and into a new dedicated delta fixture: e.g. cax.slop's cax-dw disjoint-violation example moves from `(fixture-g-disjoint-violation arena) (fixture-delta-empty arena)` to `(fixture-g-consistent arena) (fixture-delta-fido-cat arena)`; prp.slop adds fixture-delta-functional/ifp/symmetric/asymmetric/transitive/irreflexive/subprop/inverse1/inverse2/pdw to replace fixture-delta-empty in nearly every @example; scm.slop adds fixture-delta-with-class/equiv/subprop likewise. cls.slop's oneOf fixture shows the same root issue from another angle: the delta previously built its own disconnected RDF-list blank nodes (ids 10/11/12) instead of pointing at the graph fixture's actual list (ids 1/2/3), so the delta's oneOf declaration referenced structure that did not exist in the graph; the fix reuses the same blank-node ids across graph and delta fixtures. This reinforces the already-recorded \"Semi-naive delta-based fixpoint evaluation\" decision: fixtures must respect the same delta-driven trigger semantics — and shared entity identity — as production rule evaluation." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/2c302389-f358-4a27-b3a8-32852c704855> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/2c302389-f358-4a27-b3a8-32852c704855> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-01-27T22:43:01Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/2c302389-f358-4a27-b3a8-32852c704855> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Delta-based rule tests must trigger via the Delta, not the Graph" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/2c302389-f358-4a27-b3a8-32852c704855> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3f5e5977-57b0-45a1-8b9a-e544cedfd4ce> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/39f9b980-8ac5-4c0a-80fa-71efaface1d2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/39f9b980-8ac5-4c0a-80fa-71efaface1d2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Zero-init named-return locals to silence C uninitialized warnings" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/39f9b980-8ac5-4c0a-80fa-71efaface1d2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/365040dc-aee8-456c-936c-47a7dbb4c79b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/39f9b980-8ac5-4c0a-80fa-71efaface1d2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/74af8f69-d68a-4db6-a495-07bb196e4866> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/39f9b980-8ac5-4c0a-80fa-71efaface1d2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/39f9b980-8ac5-4c0a-80fa-71efaface1d2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "csrc/'s transpiled C functions use a named-return-value idiom -- `T _retval; { ... _retval = ...; ... } return _retval;` -- where the assignment happens inside a nested brace block. Even when every code path inside that block assigns _retval before the function returns, GCC/Clang can emit a \"may be used uninitialized\" warning because the assignment is not visible to the compiler's flow analysis at the point of declaration. Fix: declare with a zero-initializer, `T _retval = {0};`, at the top of the function instead of a bare declaration.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit a08a80a2ff (PR #14, \"More tests, warnings cleanup\"), third bullet \"clean up compiler warnings\". Directly observed in the diff: csrc/src/slop_cax.c (cax_apply_cax_rules, cax_cax_sco, cax_cax_eqc1, cax_cax_eqc2, cax_cax_dw, cax_cax_adc), csrc/src/slop_cls.c (cls_apply_cls_rules, cls_cls_thing, cls_cls_nothing1/2, cls_cls_int1/2, cls_cls_uni, cls_cls_com, cls_cls_svf1/2, cls_cls_avf, cls_cls_hv1/2, cls_cls_maxc1/2, cls_cls_maxqc1-4, cls_cls_oo), csrc/src/slop_common.c (common_make_parse_state, common_state_at_end, common_state_advance, common_skip_whitespace), and csrc/src/slop_dt.c (dt_dt_type1, in progress) each change `_retval;` to `_retval = {0};` with no other logic change -- purely a warning-cleanup pass. The commit's file list spans 27 files total; the same mechanical substitution is the only change visible in every hunk inspected, consistent with a repo-wide pass over this one idiom rather than a per-function behavioral fix." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/39f9b980-8ac5-4c0a-80fa-71efaface1d2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/39f9b980-8ac5-4c0a-80fa-71efaface1d2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-12T19:31:53Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/39f9b980-8ac5-4c0a-80fa-71efaface1d2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Zero-init named-return locals to silence C uninitialized warnings" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/4bd3e8da-f31e-4871-8c29-56228f92d3ce> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/4bd3e8da-f31e-4871-8c29-56228f92d3ce> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Stray CLI inferred.ttl output checked in unreferenced" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/4bd3e8da-f31e-4871-8c29-56228f92d3ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/e71422b6-0c80-4741-aa68-a27243061168> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/4bd3e8da-f31e-4871-8c29-56228f92d3ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/4bd3e8da-f31e-4871-8c29-56228f92d3ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Commit 10f2845884 (\"adding more tests\") adds cli/inferred.ttl, a 31,906-line materialized-TTL file whose first triple identifies it as reasoner output for `https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/CommonCoreOntologiesMerged` — but the file is not referenced by cli/tests/test-cli.slop, the new cli/tests/benchmark.sh, or any fixture path either file uses (benchmark.sh's own --emit test writes to /tmp/bench-out.ttl, not into the repo). `git grep -n \"inferred.ttl\" 10f2845884 -- cli` finds no references anywhere in the commit, and the file is still present, still unreferenced, at HEAD. It is most plausibly leftover scratch output from manually running the CLI's --emit flag against fixtures/CommonCoreOntologiesMerged.ttl during this commit's test development, swept into the commit by an unqualified `git add` alongside the intended benchmark.sh and fixture additions." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/4bd3e8da-f31e-4871-8c29-56228f92d3ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/4bd3e8da-f31e-4871-8c29-56228f92d3ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-07T04:53:15Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/4bd3e8da-f31e-4871-8c29-56228f92d3ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Stray CLI inferred.ttl output checked in unreferenced" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/4eb340bf-bbb6-4adc-af2c-766b7ef68570> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/4eb340bf-bbb6-4adc-af2c-766b7ef68570> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "CLI test harness arena capacity" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/4eb340bf-bbb6-4adc-af2c-766b7ef68570> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/e71422b6-0c80-4741-aa68-a27243061168> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/4eb340bf-bbb6-4adc-af2c-766b7ef68570> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/4eb340bf-bbb6-4adc-af2c-766b7ef68570> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The cli/tests/test-cli.slop integration-test runner's harness-level arena doubled from 268435456 bytes (256MB) to 536870912 bytes (512MB), because the previous 256MB allocation was no longer enough to run the full CLI test suite to completion. Evidence: commit bcaf187877 (\"test fixes\") changes test-cli.slop's `main` entry point from `(with-arena 268435456 ;; 256MB for test harness)` to `(with-arena 536870912 ;; 512MB for test harness)`, updating the trailing comment in lockstep. This harness arena backs the whole test-cli.slop suite (all fixture graphs plus the real-world-scale BFO-2020 parse/reason/serialize round trip) and is distinct from the CLI's own runtime `arena_cap`, separately noted elsewhere as needing 8GB when the BFO test is driven through the growl CLI binary directly. The commit body gives no explicit cause, but an in-place capacity doubling under a \"test fixes\" subject implies the suite was exhausting the prior 256MB harness allocation." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/4eb340bf-bbb6-4adc-af2c-766b7ef68570> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/4eb340bf-bbb6-4adc-af2c-766b7ef68570> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-05T15:56:04Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/4eb340bf-bbb6-4adc-af2c-766b7ef68570> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "CLI test harness arena capacity" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/54b79064-43f5-4aab-a8af-a4284a995890> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/54b79064-43f5-4aab-a8af-a4284a995890> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Turtle language-tag subtags need PN_CHARS, not PN_CHARS_BASE" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/54b79064-43f5-4aab-a8af-a4284a995890> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/54b79064-43f5-4aab-a8af-a4284a995890> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "ttl_parse_literal now scans the characters after each '-' in a Turtle/TTL language tag (e.g. \"en-419\") using ttl_is_pn_chars (letters + digits + '_' + '-') instead of ttl_is_pn_chars_base (letters only), so BCP47 subtags containing digits parse in full instead of truncating at the first digit.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit 79fdf0024d, csrc/src/slop_ttl.c, ttl_parse_literal's LANGTAG branch: `common_parse_while(arena, s2, (slop_closure_t){(void*)_wrap_ttl_is_pn_chars_base, NULL})` becomes `...(void*)_wrap_ttl_is_pn_chars, NULL})`. ttl_is_pn_chars_base(c) is `strlib_is_alpha(c)` (ASCII letters only; csrc/src/slop_ttl.c:1179-1181, unchanged by this commit) while ttl_is_pn_chars(c) is `ttl_is_pn_chars_base(c) || strlib_is_digit(c) || c=='_' || c=='-'` (line 1183-1185). Before this fix, a language tag like \"@en-419\" stopped scanning the subtag at the first digit; after, digit-bearing subtags parse correctly. The same commit also reorders two adjacent static wrapper-closure definitions (_wrap_ttl_is_pn_chars_base, _wrap_strlib_is_digit) with no behavioral effect — noted for completeness, not itself decision-bearing." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/54b79064-43f5-4aab-a8af-a4284a995890> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/54b79064-43f5-4aab-a8af-a4284a995890> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-13T03:03:10Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/54b79064-43f5-4aab-a8af-a4284a995890> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Turtle language-tag subtags need PN_CHARS, not PN_CHARS_BASE" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/561fc506-97c9-4975-a95c-34a61eabdd27> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/561fc506-97c9-4975-a95c-34a61eabdd27> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Drain worker channel before joining threads" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/561fc506-97c9-4975-a95c-34a61eabdd27> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/7a377274-e1bc-43a2-b657-8ae3e39fdefb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/561fc506-97c9-4975-a95c-34a61eabdd27> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/561fc506-97c9-4975-a95c-34a61eabdd27> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "collect-worker-results now receives all WorkerMessage results from the buffered result channel before calling join on the worker threads, reversing the order used in the prior (never-executed) scaffold, which joined the 5 worker threads first and only afterward drained the channel. Joining first risks deadlock on a bounded/buffered channel: a worker blocked trying to send into a full buffer never returns, so join(w) never unblocks, and the coordinator never reaches the receive loop that would free buffer space to let the send complete. Evidence: src/engine.slop diff on collect-worker-results — the comment/code block \"First join all workers to ensure they've completed\" + \"(for-each (w workers) (join w))\" placed before the channel-receive loop is removed, and a fresh \"(for-each (w workers) (join w))\" (comment: \"Join all workers to ensure they've completed\") is added after the receive loop instead." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/561fc506-97c9-4975-a95c-34a61eabdd27> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/561fc506-97c9-4975-a95c-34a61eabdd27> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-06T04:49:33Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/561fc506-97c9-4975-a95c-34a61eabdd27> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Drain worker channel before joining threads" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/561fc506-97c9-4975-a95c-34a61eabdd27> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/46b6eb2f-386e-47d1-82f6-6aed459402e6> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/78024597-a768-4a8e-a116-1201ec2f5507> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/78024597-a768-4a8e-a116-1201ec2f5507> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Reasonable's reason() returns full closure, not delta" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/78024597-a768-4a8e-a116-1201ec2f5507> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/e71422b6-0c80-4741-aa68-a27243061168> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/78024597-a768-4a8e-a116-1201ec2f5507> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/78024597-a768-4a8e-a116-1201ec2f5507> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The Python `reasonable` package's `PyReasoner.reason()` returns the FULL materialized closure (base graph + inferred triples), not just newly-inferred triples — so `cli/tests/benchmark_compare.py`'s prior `output_count = input_count + len(triples)` double-counted every echoed base triple as if it were newly inferred, inflating Reasonable's reported inferred/total counts and therefore its accuracy-divergence percentages in the README benchmark table.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit 7b8193392d (\"benchmark fixes\"). `run_reasonable()` (cli/tests/benchmark_compare.py:67) now captures `base = set(g)` right after parsing, and the fix comment states it directly: \"reason() returns the FULL materialized closure (base + inferred), not just new triples -- so output_count = input_count + len(triples) would double-count the echoed base.\" The corrected line is `output_count = input_count + len(set(triples) - base)`." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/78024597-a768-4a8e-a116-1201ec2f5507> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/78024597-a768-4a8e-a116-1201ec2f5507> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-29T18:50:33Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/78024597-a768-4a8e-a116-1201ec2f5507> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Reasonable's reason() returns full closure, not delta" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/78024597-a768-4a8e-a116-1201ec2f5507> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f3641e03-9d08-42da-8abc-0eaa4e24930e> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8f5b5407-7784-4c9f-8d6d-df20fb5f87e9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8f5b5407-7784-4c9f-8d6d-df20fb5f87e9> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Don't return printf's result as a function's status code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8f5b5407-7784-4c9f-8d6d-df20fb5f87e9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/e71422b6-0c80-4741-aa68-a27243061168> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8f5b5407-7784-4c9f-8d6d-df20fb5f87e9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8f5b5407-7784-4c9f-8d6d-df20fb5f87e9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "csrc/src/slop_main.c's TTL-parse-failure switch (the parse_error/file_error arms added by \"CLI reports TTL parse error line/column\") used `return printf(...)` to end each case, which makes main() exit with printf's return value — the count of bytes written (e.g. the length of the error message) — as the process's exit status, instead of a real status code. This commit replaces both `return printf(...)` with `printf(...); break;`, letting execution fall through to the existing `return 1;` after the switch so the CLI now exits 1 consistently on either parse error or file error.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit 9df6bffce5 diff on csrc/src/slop_main.c, case ttl_TtlFileError_parse_error and case ttl_TtlFileError_file_error: `return printf(\"%.*s\\n\", ...)` and `return printf(\"%s\\n\", \"  (file error)\")` become `printf(...); break;` in both arms, with the pre-existing `return 1;` immediately following the switch now reachable." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8f5b5407-7784-4c9f-8d6d-df20fb5f87e9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8f5b5407-7784-4c9f-8d6d-df20fb5f87e9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-11T19:58:48Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8f5b5407-7784-4c9f-8d6d-df20fb5f87e9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Don't return printf's result as a function's status code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8f5b5407-7784-4c9f-8d6d-df20fb5f87e9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4ad1543a-b52a-4caa-9752-ca7ee85f7e8a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/90721289-ec22-49be-821a-9404db845e78> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/90721289-ec22-49be-821a-9404db845e78> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "indexed-graph-add / delta-add return updated value, not mutate" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/90721289-ec22-49be-821a-9404db845e78> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/365040dc-aee8-456c-936c-47a7dbb4c79b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/90721289-ec22-49be-821a-9404db845e78> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/90721289-ec22-49be-821a-9404db845e78> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "indexed-graph-add and delta-add do not mutate their Graph/Delta argument in place — they return a new/updated value that the caller must capture. Prior to this commit, rule-module test fixtures across cax.slop, cls.slop, eq.slop, prp.slop, and scm.slop bound a local `(let ((g (indexed-graph-create arena)) ...) (indexed-graph-add arena g triple) ... g)` without ever reassigning `g`/`d`, so every indexed-graph-add/delta-add call's result was silently discarded and the fixture actually returned an empty graph/delta. Commit 7b74989 (\"fix the growl tests!\") fixes this by declaring the binding `mut` and threading the result through `(set! g (indexed-graph-add arena g triple))` (and the equivalent for delta-add) for every add call, across all five rule modules' fixture-g-*/fixture-delta-* functions. Evidence: diff hunks in src/rules/cax.slop, cls.slop, eq.slop, prp.slop, scm.slop — every affected fixture function changes `(let ((g ...) ...) (indexed-graph-add ...) ... g)` to `(let ((mut g ...) ...) (set! g (indexed-graph-add ...)) ... g)`. Consequence: rule-module @example test fixtures now actually build graphs/deltas containing the intended triples, so example results reflect true rule behavior instead of silently evaluating against empty structures." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/90721289-ec22-49be-821a-9404db845e78> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/90721289-ec22-49be-821a-9404db845e78> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-01-27T22:43:01Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/90721289-ec22-49be-821a-9404db845e78> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "indexed-graph-add / delta-add return updated value, not mutate" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/95f981e8-b25c-4b3a-91f8-be694205955b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/95f981e8-b25c-4b3a-91f8-be694205955b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Force-link -sys crates via extern crate marker" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/95f981e8-b25c-4b3a-91f8-be694205955b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/833a482a-9217-4511-99e7-1166a8c28fbb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/95f981e8-b25c-4b3a-91f8-be694205955b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/95f981e8-b25c-4b3a-91f8-be694205955b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "When a Rust crate consumes a -sys crate's native library only through C code (FFI symbol calls from vendored .c files), rustc's dead-crate elimination will drop that `--extern` crate — and the native static archive bundled inside its rlib — from the final link if no Rust source in the crate otherwise names it, leaving the C symbols the vendored code calls undefined at link time. growl's own C code (csrc/src/*.c) calls directly into slop-rdf-sys's and slop-std-sys's C symbols (vocab_*, rdf_*, xsd_*, strlib_*, ...), but nothing in rust/src's Rust source otherwise names either crate, so rust/src/lib.rs adds `extern crate slop_rdf_sys as _; extern crate slop_std_sys as _;` markers purely to force-link them.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit c9a80f902b's rust/src/lib.rs diff adds this exact two-line marker with a comment explaining: \"Nothing in this crate's *Rust* source otherwise names either crate, so without this marker rustc's dead-crate-elimination drops both `--extern` crates -- and the native archives bundled inside their rlibs -- from the final binary link, leaving those C symbols undefined at link time.\"" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/95f981e8-b25c-4b3a-91f8-be694205955b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/95f981e8-b25c-4b3a-91f8-be694205955b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-10T18:10:28Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/95f981e8-b25c-4b3a-91f8-be694205955b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Force-link -sys crates via extern crate marker" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/95f981e8-b25c-4b3a-91f8-be694205955b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0950df26-7f03-4085-84fb-523dc9b7145a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/a5c3bbc3-5a36-4d5b-bb08-8cb507c5027c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/a5c3bbc3-5a36-4d5b-bb08-8cb507c5027c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "RDF-star quoted triples need recursion in blank-node bookkeeping" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/a5c3bbc3-5a36-4d5b-bb08-8cb507c5027c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/9f7a7679-6c17-40b2-bbef-b78d9832bfa1> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/a5c3bbc3-5a36-4d5b-bb08-8cb507c5027c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/e71422b6-0c80-4741-aa68-a27243061168> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/a5c3bbc3-5a36-4d5b-bb08-8cb507c5027c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/a5c3bbc3-5a36-4d5b-bb08-8cb507c5027c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "growl's own blank-node bookkeeping functions (remap-blank-term, max-blank-id-in-graph, src/growl.slop) must recurse into nested RDF-star quoted-triple terms (the term-triple variant), not just handle blank/iri/literal at the top level — otherwise blank IDs nested inside a quoted triple used as a triple's subject/predicate/object are silently invisible to max-ID computation and never get remapped, which can cause blank-ID collisions when a --background ontology containing RDF-star reification is merged (per \"Background ontology blank nodes need remapping before merge\"). A second, independent gap in the same functions: max-blank-id-in-graph never scanned the predicate position at all (only subject/object), even before RDF-star existed.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit 22e3b476 (\"Adopt RDF 1.2 quoted triple terms from slop-rdf\", 2026-06-26) added rdf_Term's 4th term-triple variant and its Consequence already flagged that every rdf_Term-tag switch in csrc/ needed a matching arm — but that consequence was about the *vendored* slop-rdf library's own eq/hash functions regenerating cleanly. growl's own hand-written helpers in src/growl.slop are not regenerated from slop-rdf, so they were missed: remap-blank-term's match only had term-blank/term-iri/term-literal arms, and max-blank-id-in-graph inlined `(match (. t subject) ((term-blank b) ...) (_ (do)))` for subject and object only. Both compiled fine (no missing-arm error) but were functionally silent for term-triple, so the gap shipped unnoticed from 2026-06-26 until this commit (9d5a603a56, \"RDF-1.2 fix / New rust vendor build\", 2026-08-10), which adds a new max-blank-id-in-term helper with a term-triple arm recursing into subject/predicate/object, gives remap-blank-term a matching term-triple arm, rewrites max-blank-id-in-graph to call the new helper across subject/predicate/object, and adds cli/tests/test-cli.slop's test-rdf-star-blank-remapping regression test (nested blank ids 2/7 inside a quoted triple, remapped by offset 10, checked against max-blank-id-in-graph and term-eq on the remapped structure). growl's own version (slop.toml) and its Rust crate (rust/Cargo.toml) both bump 0.6.1 -> 0.7.0 to ship the fix.</description>\n<parameter name=\"status\">accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/a5c3bbc3-5a36-4d5b-bb08-8cb507c5027c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/a5c3bbc3-5a36-4d5b-bb08-8cb507c5027c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-10T18:38:13Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
