<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/163f7502-c7c1-49d9-b531-7f129f5b42df> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The new cli/tests/test-cli.slop suite drives the full parse -> reason -> report/emit pipeline through the CLI's own code paths (not direct engine/rule-module calls) against a set of small single-concern TTL fixtures (subclass-chain, equivalent-class, disjoint-violation, sameas-chain, sameas-differentfrom, empty) AND, distinctly, a full real-world ontology: cli/tests/fixtures/bfo-core.ttl (BFO 2020, 1227 lines). test-bfo-consistent is called out in main's comments as \"Real-world ontology test (requires 8GB arena_cap)\" and is run first in the suite. This establishes real-world-scale ontology testing (BFO) as part of growl's test strategy, distinct from and in addition to the existing synthetic per-rule @example fixtures in src/rules/. Evidence: commit c12cd0ed (\"getting bfo test working\") adds cli/tests/test-cli.slop's module doc \"Tests the full pipeline: parse TTL -> reason -> report/emit\" plus test-bfo-consistent and the bfo-core.ttl fixture." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
