<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/1d0b710d-5add-40e6-9562-3c5fe9a6f952> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/1d0b710d-5add-40e6-9562-3c5fe9a6f952> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Z3-verifiable design-by-contract on every function" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/1d0b710d-5add-40e6-9562-3c5fe9a6f952> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/365040dc-aee8-456c-936c-47a7dbb4c79b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/1d0b710d-5add-40e6-9562-3c5fe9a6f952> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/7a377274-e1bc-43a2-b657-8ae3e39fdefb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/1d0b710d-5add-40e6-9562-3c5fe9a6f952> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/1d0b710d-5add-40e6-9562-3c5fe9a6f952> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Every function across growl's modules carries @intent/@spec/@pre/@post/@alloc/@example annotations (e.g. engine-run's @post bounding iterations by config.max-iterations, delta-add's postcondition on iteration invariance) intended for SMT (Z3) verification via slop.toml's [verify] section (pattern=\"*.slop\", sources=[\"src\"], timeout=5000ms per file). Formal contract verification, not just runtime tests, is the primary correctness discipline for reasoner rules — both growl.slop and engine.slop module docs advertise \"Z3-verifiable\"/\"formally verified contracts\"." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/1d0b710d-5add-40e6-9562-3c5fe9a6f952> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
