<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/5fc9701f-7647-4521-9159-a0639b28f176> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/5fc9701f-7647-4521-9159-a0639b28f176> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Per-rule OWL 2 RL conformance test suite" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/5fc9701f-7647-4521-9159-a0639b28f176> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/365040dc-aee8-456c-936c-47a7dbb4c79b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/5fc9701f-7647-4521-9159-a0639b28f176> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/74af8f69-d68a-4db6-a495-07bb196e4866> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/5fc9701f-7647-4521-9159-a0639b28f176> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/e71422b6-0c80-4741-aa68-a27243061168> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/5fc9701f-7647-4521-9159-a0639b28f176> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/5fc9701f-7647-4521-9159-a0639b28f176> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Growl gains a dedicated pytest suite, cli/tests/test_conformance.py (792 lines), that tests each OWL 2 RL rule individually rather than through synthetic pipeline fixtures or an external reference-reasoner diff: for each rule it writes a minimal Turtle premise (via a shared PREFIXES header for rdf/rdfs/owl/xsd/t:), runs `growl --quiet --complete --emit <out> <premise>` as a subprocess through a shared `run_growl` helper, and either parses the emitted Turtle with rdflib to assert the expected entailment triple is present, or asserts the process exits with rc=1 for premises constructed to be inconsistent. The module docstring states it covers \"each of the 76 OWL 2 RL rules,\" organized by spec table: Table 4 equality (9 rules: eq-ref, eq-sym, eq-trans, eq-rep-s/p/o, eq-diff1-3, differentFrom symmetry), Table 5 property axioms (20: prp-ap, prp-dom, prp-rng, prp-fp, prp-ifp, prp-irp, prp-symp, prp-asyp, prp-trp, prp-spo1/2, prp-eqp1/2, prp-pdw, prp-adp, prp-inv1/2, prp-key, prp-npa1/2), Table 6 class expressions (19: cls-thing, cls-nothing1/2, cls-int1/2, cls-uni, cls-com, cls-svf1/2, cls-avf, cls-hv1/2, cls-maxc1/2, cls-maxqc1-4, cls-oo), Table 7 class axioms (5: cax-sco, cax-eqc1/2, cax-dw, cax-adc), Table 8 datatypes (3: dt-type1/2, dt-not-type), and Table 9 schema vocabulary (20: scm-cls, scm-sco, scm-eqc1/2, scm-op, scm-dp, scm-spo, scm-eqp1/2, scm-dom1/2, scm-rng1/2, scm-hv, scm-svf1/2, scm-avf1/2, plus others). It deliberately uses growl's `--complete` mode, the flag whose prior rationale was specifically \"for conformance testing against other reasoners like owlrl.\" It is wired into the build as a new `make conformance` target (`conformance: release`, added to .PHONY) running `cd cli/tests && uv run --with pytest --with rdflib pytest test_conformance.py test_interactions.py -v` — the first Makefile target to invoke a Python test suite directly via `uv run --with`'s ephemeral dependency resolution, rather than requiring a separately `pip install`-ed environment as the pre-existing benchmark_compare.py script does. .gitignore gains `__pycache__` in the same commit, consistent with introducing this pytest-based tooling.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit 962ad5b8c7 (\"added conformance tests (#13)\") adds cli/tests/test_conformance.py in full; Makefile diff hunk adds the `conformance` target and widens .PHONY; .gitignore diff hunk adds `__pycache__`." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
