<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/89aed80f-adc9-42b2-b313-7c3bb44e788e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/89aed80f-adc9-42b2-b313-7c3bb44e788e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "FFI layout guard tests via C shim sizeof/offsetof exports" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/89aed80f-adc9-42b2-b313-7c3bb44e788e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/74af8f69-d68a-4db6-a495-07bb196e4866> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/89aed80f-adc9-42b2-b313-7c3bb44e788e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/833a482a-9217-4511-99e7-1166a8c28fbb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/89aed80f-adc9-42b2-b313-7c3bb44e788e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/89aed80f-adc9-42b2-b313-7c3bb44e788e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "rust/csrc_shim.c now exports a set of `growl_layout_*` functions (growl_layout_sizeof_triple_index, growl_layout_sizeof_indexed_graph, growl_layout_offset_graph_size, growl_layout_sizeof_rdf_term, growl_layout_sizeof_rdf_triple, growl_layout_sizeof_reasoner_config, growl_layout_offset_cfg_cancel_ptr, growl_layout_sizeof_reasoner_success, growl_layout_offset_success_iterations) that report the real C `sizeof`/`offsetof` of the C-ABI structs (index_TripleIndex, index_IndexedGraph, rdf_Term, rdf_Triple, types_ReasonerConfig, types_ReasonerSuccess) at runtime, and rust/src/ffi.rs gains a `#[cfg(test)] mod layout_guard` with an `ffi_structs_match_c_abi` test asserting `core::mem::size_of`/`offset_of!` on every hand-written #[repr(C)] mirror (TripleIndex, IndexedGraphFfi, RdfTerm, RdfTriple, ReasonerConfigFfi, ReasonerSuccessFfi) equals the corresponding C-reported value. This establishes a recurring, applicable-to-any-future-struct-change technique for catching FFI ABI drift at `cargo test` time instead of at runtime, motivated directly by the \"Hand-written Rust FFI struct mirrors silently drift from the C ABI\" lesson.\n\nEvidence: commit ef9ac8a9eb (\"ABI fix\") diff on rust/csrc_shim.c (new \"FFI layout guards\" section with header comment citing the 0.6.0 regression) and rust/src/ffi.rs (new `extern \"C\"` declarations for the growl_layout_* functions plus the `layout_guard` test module, whose doc comment states \"Assert the hand-written #[repr(C)] mirrors in this module match the real C ABI reported by csrc_shim.c\")." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/89aed80f-adc9-42b2-b313-7c3bb44e788e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/89aed80f-adc9-42b2-b313-7c3bb44e788e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-29T22:51:53Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
