<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/957a1113-fffb-4a0d-8492-dbde492b72d6> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "OWL-RL reference comparison harness" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/957a1113-fffb-4a0d-8492-dbde492b72d6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/365040dc-aee8-456c-936c-47a7dbb4c79b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/957a1113-fffb-4a0d-8492-dbde492b72d6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/e71422b6-0c80-4741-aa68-a27243061168> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/957a1113-fffb-4a0d-8492-dbde492b72d6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/957a1113-fffb-4a0d-8492-dbde492b72d6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "cli/tests/benchmark_compare.py is a new Python script that runs the W3C reference OWL 2 RL/RDF implementation (the `owlrl` package's `DeductiveClosure(OWLRL_Semantics)`) as ground truth against growl's own `--fast` and full-mode CLI output, over the same fixture set used by the existing shell benchmark (bfo-core.ttl, pizza.ttl, CommonCoreOntologiesMerged.ttl, schemaorg.ttl, Brick.ttl), reporting each reasoner's input/inferred/total triple counts and timing, plus the delta between growl's inferred count and OWL-RL's for both modes. This establishes an external, independently-implemented correctness baseline distinct from growl's own synthetic @example fixtures and the existing BFO/benchmark-scale suites, at the cost of requiring `pip install owlrl rdflib` and being too slow (pure Python) to run over the largest fixtures (skipped above 20000 input triples).\n\nWhy + evidence: commit d26d5120 (merge PR #3 \"Completing\") adds cli/tests/benchmark_compare.py (173 lines) with the module docstring \"Reasoner comparison: OWL-RL (ground truth) vs Growl... OWL-RL is the W3C reference implementation for OWL 2 RL/RDF rules. It serves as ground truth for expected inference counts.\" It skips OWL-RL (not growl) above a 20000-input-triple threshold since \"OWL-RL is pure Python and very slow on large files,\" and runs each growl invocation 3 times, taking the median, by parsing growl's `--quiet` one-line summary output." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/957a1113-fffb-4a0d-8492-dbde492b72d6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/957a1113-fffb-4a0d-8492-dbde492b72d6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-08T00:55:37Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
