<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/9a9ff924-a3a6-4102-82af-eb4059b93813> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/9a9ff924-a3a6-4102-82af-eb4059b93813> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Eleven InconsistencyReport-returning rule functions across src/rules/{cax,cls,dt,eq,prp}.slop gain a second @post clause asserting a rule-specific minimum on (list-len (. r witnesses)) in the (some r) case, supplementing the pre-existing generic \"(string-len (. report reason)) > 0\" postcondition with a machine-checked lower bound on evidence size: cax-dw and cls-com require >=3 witnesses; cax-adc, eq-diff1, eq-diff2, eq-diff3, and prp-asyp require >=2; cls-nothing2, dt-not-type, and prp-irp require >=1; prp-pdw was given >=2 by this commit (a later commit raises it further to >=3). Evidence: commit 535cc1e (PR #5 \"more_contracts\", \"More contracts\") diff hunks adding a second (@post (match $result ((none) true) ((some r) (>= (list-len (. r witnesses)) N)))) block immediately after the existing reason-length @post in each of these eleven functions." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/9a9ff924-a3a6-4102-82af-eb4059b93813> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
