<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/a53ee554-4bdb-4138-87e0-65533a7bbf50> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rule modules mirror OWL 2 RL spec tables" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/a53ee554-4bdb-4138-87e0-65533a7bbf50> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/365040dc-aee8-456c-936c-47a7dbb4c79b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/a53ee554-4bdb-4138-87e0-65533a7bbf50> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/a53ee554-4bdb-4138-87e0-65533a7bbf50> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Each inference-rule module and function is named after its W3C OWL 2 RL specification table/rule ID for direct spec traceability: eq.slop = Table 4 (equality: eq-sym, eq-trans, eq-rep-s/p/o, eq-diff1-3), prp.slop = Table 5 (property axioms: prp-dom, prp-fp, prp-trp, ...), cls.slop = Table 6 (class expressions: cls-int1, cls-svf1, cls-maxc1, ...), cax.slop = Table 7 (class axioms: cax-sco, cax-eqc1, cax-dw, cax-adc), scm.slop = Table 9 (schema vocabulary: scm-cls, scm-sco, scm-spo, ...). Each module's header comment cites the corresponding table number and the W3C spec URL." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/a53ee554-4bdb-4138-87e0-65533a7bbf50> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/a53ee554-4bdb-4138-87e0-65533a7bbf50> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-01-27T01:30:15Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/a53ee554-4bdb-4138-87e0-65533a7bbf50> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rule modules mirror OWL 2 RL spec tables" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/b75f06b5-7d02-491d-9f13-5d8e41bdaa8e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/b75f06b5-7d02-491d-9f13-5d8e41bdaa8e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "CLI benchmark suite across real-world-scale ontologies" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/b75f06b5-7d02-491d-9f13-5d8e41bdaa8e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/e71422b6-0c80-4741-aa68-a27243061168> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/b75f06b5-7d02-491d-9f13-5d8e41bdaa8e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/b75f06b5-7d02-491d-9f13-5d8e41bdaa8e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "growl gains a standalone shell benchmark harness, cli/tests/benchmark.sh, distinct from the correctness-oriented cli/tests/test-cli.slop integration suite (see \"CLI integration tests against real and synthetic TTL fixtures\"): it runs the built growl CLI three times each, for timing stability, over consistent fixtures of increasing scale (fixtures/empty.ttl, fixtures/bfo-core.ttl, benchmarks/pizza.ttl, fixtures/CommonCoreOntologiesMerged.ttl, benchmarks/Brick.ttl, benchmarks/schemaorg.ttl), once for an --emit serialization test (writing to /tmp/bench-out.ttl, not into the repo), and once each over a new set of small benchmarks/*-inconsistent.ttl fixtures (bfo, brick, pizza) to confirm inconsistency is still detected at benchmark scale. Evidence: commit 10f2845884 adds cli/tests/benchmark.sh (63 lines) plus cli/tests/fixtures/benchmarks/{pizza.ttl (1906 lines), Brick.ttl (48827 lines), schemaorg.ttl (21562 lines), bfo-inconsistent.ttl, brick-inconsistent.ttl, pizza-inconsistent.ttl}; the script gracefully SKIPs any fixture path (e.g. fixtures/CommonCoreOntologiesMerged.ttl, added earlier in commit ee866f6) that isn't present rather than failing." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/b75f06b5-7d02-491d-9f13-5d8e41bdaa8e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/b75f06b5-7d02-491d-9f13-5d8e41bdaa8e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-07T04:53:15Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/b75f06b5-7d02-491d-9f13-5d8e41bdaa8e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "CLI benchmark suite across real-world-scale ontologies" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/f07a7722-b585-4e1c-8661-69487856f186> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/f07a7722-b585-4e1c-8661-69487856f186> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Reference reasoner completeness test suite" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/f07a7722-b585-4e1c-8661-69487856f186> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/365040dc-aee8-456c-936c-47a7dbb4c79b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/f07a7722-b585-4e1c-8661-69487856f186> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/74af8f69-d68a-4db6-a495-07bb196e4866> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/f07a7722-b585-4e1c-8661-69487856f186> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/e71422b6-0c80-4741-aa68-a27243061168> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/f07a7722-b585-4e1c-8661-69487856f186> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/f07a7722-b585-4e1c-8661-69487856f186> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Growl gains cli/tests/test_reference.py, a new pytest suite that runs the W3C reference owlrl package's DeductiveClosure(OWLRL_Semantics) over real ontology fixtures and asserts Growl's `--complete` CLI output contains every comparable named triple that owlrl's closure produces (zero missing); extra triples Growl produces beyond owlrl are logged but do NOT fail the test -- exact triple-set equality (failing on extras too) was implicitly rejected in favor of this asymmetric missing-only assertion.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit a08a80a2ff (PR #14, \"More tests, warnings cleanup\"), first bullet \"reference test against owlrl\". New file cli/tests/test_reference.py (169 lines) parametrizes test_reference_no_missing over ONTOLOGIES = [bfo-core.ttl, benchmarks/pizza.ttl, equivalent-class.ttl, sameas-chain.ttl, subclass-chain.ttl]; for each it runs run_owlrl() (rdflib parse + DeductiveClosure) and run_growl() (subprocess `growl --quiet --complete --emit <tmp> <path>`, parsed back with rdflib), computes `missing = owlrl_set - growl_set` after filtering through is_comparable()/normalize_triple(), and asserts len(missing) == 0. is_comparable() explicitly excludes: blank-node subjects/objects (different skolemization across systems), literal-subject triples (owlrl's eq-ref/dt-type2 produce these but they can't be serialized in Turtle), reflexive owl:sameAs (trivial tautologies, already covered by eq-ref in the per-rule conformance suite), and datatype owl:disjointWith (an owlrl extension not required by the OWL 2 RL spec tables); normalize_triple() collapses plain-literal vs xsd:string literal differences per RDF 1.1 equivalence. The Makefile gains a new `reference: release` target (`cd cli/tests && uv run --with pytest --with rdflib --with owlrl pytest test_reference.py -v`) and `reference` is added to .PHONY; README.md's build-commands block documents both `make conformance` and `make reference` (the latter as \"accuracy tests against OWL-RL reference reasoner\").\n\nThis is distinct from the pre-existing \"OWL-RL reference comparison harness\" (benchmark_compare.py), which reports triple-count/timing deltas rather than asserting per-triple correctness, and from the \"Per-rule OWL 2 RL conformance test suite\" (test_conformance.py), which uses minimal synthetic per-rule premises rather than real multi-rule-interaction ontologies.\n\nConsequence: over-inference (extra/spurious triples Growl produces beyond owlrl's closure) is not caught by this suite -- only missing (under-inferred) entailments fail it. Blank-node-involving and literal-subject entailments are excluded from this reference-comparison approach entirely, so their correctness still relies on the per-rule conformance suite and BFO/CCO integration tests, not this suite." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/f07a7722-b585-4e1c-8661-69487856f186> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/f07a7722-b585-4e1c-8661-69487856f186> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-12T19:31:53Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/f07a7722-b585-4e1c-8661-69487856f186> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Reference reasoner completeness test suite" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/07543f68-aecb-4213-8a9d-a298b7095d56> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/07543f68-aecb-4213-8a9d-a298b7095d56> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "later-decision" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/07543f68-aecb-4213-8a9d-a298b7095d56> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Reasonable accuracy divergence re-measured (owlrl 7.1.4)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/07543f68-aecb-4213-8a9d-a298b7095d56> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/07543f68-aecb-4213-8a9d-a298b7095d56> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "This commit's README diff updates the Accuracy table's Reasonable-column percentages in place and adds an explicit methodology note (\"Measured with owlrl 7.1.4 and reasonable 0.4.4 — reasoner versions can shift inference counts, so the Reasonable column reflects that release specifically\") explaining why: the reference/comparison tool versions moved since the prior snapshot, so the old percentages no longer reflect the current measured comparison. This also explains why the Growl-mode columns shifted slightly too (e.g. BFO Growl --complete -0.7%→-0.6%), since all percentages are computed against the same owlrl-derived reference count, which itself moved with the tool bump." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/07543f68-aecb-4213-8a9d-a298b7095d56> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/07543f68-aecb-4213-8a9d-a298b7095d56> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-29T17:11:16Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/07543f68-aecb-4213-8a9d-a298b7095d56> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Reasonable accuracy divergence re-measured (owlrl 7.1.4)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/0bf4a2e9-c8eb-4080-83e9-3cbb023b700f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/0bf4a2e9-c8eb-4080-83e9-3cbb023b700f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Local/manual builds now report the slop.toml-derived version by default" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/0bf4a2e9-c8eb-4080-83e9-3cbb023b700f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/0bf4a2e9-c8eb-4080-83e9-3cbb023b700f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Commit 19d065eac6 (\"Makefile fix\") changes the Makefile's `GROWL_VERSION ?= 0.1.0` default to `GROWL_VERSION ?= $(shell sed -n 's/^version = \"\\(.*\\)\"/\\1/p' slop.toml | head -1)`, so the earlier consequence (\"local/manual builds silently default to the placeholder 0.1.0 unless GROWL_VERSION is passed explicitly ... misleading version string\") no longer holds: an unadorned `make cli`/`make test`/`make lib`/`make release` now reports slop.toml's actual [project] version (e.g. \"0.7.0\") instead of a stale placeholder. The tag-triggered release workflow's explicit `make release GROWL_VERSION=$VERSION` override is untouched and still takes precedence." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/0bf4a2e9-c8eb-4080-83e9-3cbb023b700f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/0bf4a2e9-c8eb-4080-83e9-3cbb023b700f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-29T17:25:47Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/0bf4a2e9-c8eb-4080-83e9-3cbb023b700f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Local/manual builds now report the slop.toml-derived version by default" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/112a81fc-4963-4576-91ac-7ab283fb4d7b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/112a81fc-4963-4576-91ac-7ab283fb4d7b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "later-decision" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/112a81fc-4963-4576-91ac-7ab283fb4d7b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Fast mode gains scm-sco/scm-eqc1 schema closure" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/112a81fc-4963-4576-91ac-7ab283fb4d7b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/112a81fc-4963-4576-91ac-7ab283fb4d7b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The superseded decision stated \"`--fast` still skips scm-* (schema vocabulary)\" entirely. This commit retires that clause: `--fast` now runs scm-sco (subClassOf transitive closure) and scm-eqc1/scm-eqc1b (equivalentClass -> subClassOf) via a new dedicated `engine_schema_materialize_fast` path, specifically to mirror the `reasonable` reference reasoner's own rule coverage -- the benchmark comparison partner introduced by \"Reasonable added to benchmark comparison harness\". It still skips the remaining schema rules (scm-op/dp/eqp/int/uni/dom/rng/svf/avf/hv), datatype rules, eq-diff1/2/3, eq-ref, and cardinality rules; the consistency-check-runs-unconditionally part of the superseded decision is unaffected and carries forward.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit 7b8193392d (\"benchmark fixes\"). README's Fast Mode section changes to: \"It runs the property and class rules plus scm-sco ... and scm-eqc1 ..., and skips the remaining schema vocabulary rules ... It deliberately does not replicate Reasonable's non-standard typing of every entity as owl:Thing.\" csrc/src/slop_engine.c adds `engine_schema_materialize_fast(arena, g)` (declared slop_engine.h:16, defined slop_engine.c:1054), which runs `scm_scm_eqc1`, `scm_scm_eqc1b`, then `engine_compute_tc` over `rdfs:subClassOf`. `engine_engine_run`'s materialization dispatch changes from `((config.fast || config.enrich)) ? initial : engine_schema_materialize(...)` to `(config.enrich) ? initial : ((config.fast) ? engine_schema_materialize_fast(arena, initial) : engine_schema_materialize(...))` -- so fast mode now takes its own materialization path distinct from enrich, instead of sharing enrich's \"skip materialization entirely\" path. The README also newly frames --fast's purpose narrowly: \"it exists mainly for that benchmark comparison rather than everyday use (use the default mode for real work).\"" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/112a81fc-4963-4576-91ac-7ab283fb4d7b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/112a81fc-4963-4576-91ac-7ab283fb4d7b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-29T18:50:33Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/112a81fc-4963-4576-91ac-7ab283fb4d7b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Fast mode gains scm-sco/scm-eqc1 schema closure" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1179d4ae-d02c-4c63-9ab8-0de8c869205e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1179d4ae-d02c-4c63-9ab8-0de8c869205e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: dt-type2 literal typing in Complete Mode" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1179d4ae-d02c-4c63-9ab8-0de8c869205e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1179d4ae-d02c-4c63-9ab8-0de8c869205e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The prior \"Opt-in --complete mode plus partial dt-* validation\" decision explicitly stated dt-type2, dt-eq, and dt-diff remain unimplemented. This commit implements dt-type2, gated behind the existing opt-in --complete flag consistent with that decision's gating pattern for zero-practical-value conformance rules, raising coverage from 75/78 (96%) to 76/78 (97%). dt-eq and dt-diff remain unimplemented and are unaffected." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1179d4ae-d02c-4c63-9ab8-0de8c869205e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1179d4ae-d02c-4c63-9ab8-0de8c869205e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-09T06:09:50Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1179d4ae-d02c-4c63-9ab8-0de8c869205e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: dt-type2 literal typing in Complete Mode" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/28bdd8f8-ba11-4237-893f-654804a1c8ec> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/28bdd8f8-ba11-4237-893f-654804a1c8ec> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "record-was-inaccurate" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/28bdd8f8-ba11-4237-893f-654804a1c8ec> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Reasonable accuracy re-measured after double-count fix" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/28bdd8f8-ba11-4237-893f-654804a1c8ec> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/28bdd8f8-ba11-4237-893f-654804a1c8ec> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The superseded Consequence's percentages were computed with the double-counting bug in `run_reasonable()` (Reasonable's inferred count included every echoed base triple as if newly inferred -- see Lesson \"Reasonable's reason() returns full closure, not delta\"). This commit fixes that counting bug AND changes what --fast itself infers (see ArchitecturalDecision \"Fast mode gains scm-sco/scm-eqc1 schema closure\"), so both the Reasonable column and the Growl --fast column of the Accuracy table move, and per the new README paragraph the two now \"track closely\" instead of Reasonable being wildly separated from every other measurement.\n\nWhy + evidence: commit 7b8193392d (\"benchmark fixes\") README.md diff -- Accuracy table Reasonable column changes BFO -34.3%->-75.6%, Pizza -64.0%->-88.3%, CCO -34.8%->-59.9%, Schema.org +28.7%->-15.8%, Brick +104.2%->-29.9%; Growl --fast column changes -83.7%->-76.6%, -95.2%->-91.2%, -76.0%->-51.5%, -40.5%->-27.7%, -69.5%->-47.2%. New paragraph: \"Reasonable's reason() returns the full materialized closure, so its inferred count is closure-minus-input (counting input + len(reason()) would double-count the echoed base). With that corrected and --fast carrying Reasonable's schema rules, the two now track closely (Growl --fast vs Reasonable: BFO -22, Pizza -231, CCO +4,372, Schema.org -3,175, Brick -6,824). The residual is mostly Reasonable's non-standard typing of every entity as owl:Thing, which --fast does not emit.\"" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/28bdd8f8-ba11-4237-893f-654804a1c8ec> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/28bdd8f8-ba11-4237-893f-654804a1c8ec> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-29T18:50:33Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/28bdd8f8-ba11-4237-893f-654804a1c8ec> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Reasonable accuracy re-measured after double-count fix" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2afc6997-2cd9-4b47-812c-e08279add5bc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2afc6997-2cd9-4b47-812c-e08279add5bc> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "later-decision" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2afc6997-2cd9-4b47-812c-e08279add5bc> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: 12 coordinator-owned 1MB arenas, sub-divided within rule groups, per parallel iteration" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2afc6997-2cd9-4b47-812c-e08279add5bc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2afc6997-2cd9-4b47-812c-e08279add5bc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Commit 10f2845884 (\"adding more tests\") changes src/engine.slop's apply-all-rules-parallel from allocating 5 coordinator-owned 1MB arenas (one per rule group: arena-scm/cax/prp/eq/cls) to allocating 12 (arena-scm-class, arena-scm-prop, arena-scm-domrng, arena-cax-infer, arena-cax-check, arena-prp-char, arena-prp-chain, arena-prp-check, arena-eq-infer, arena-eq-check, arena-cls-set, arena-cls-ind), matching the new 12-way sub-worker partitioning (see \"Semantic sub-worker partitioning for parallel rule dispatch\")." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2afc6997-2cd9-4b47-812c-e08279add5bc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2afc6997-2cd9-4b47-812c-e08279add5bc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-07T04:53:15Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/2afc6997-2cd9-4b47-812c-e08279add5bc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: 12 coordinator-owned 1MB arenas, sub-divided within rule groups, per parallel iteration" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/372548de-05b7-4bb1-8083-eb85bb6f913e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/372548de-05b7-4bb1-8083-eb85bb6f913e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "later-decision" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/372548de-05b7-4bb1-8083-eb85bb6f913e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Rust Arena must stay !Send + !Sync" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/372548de-05b7-4bb1-8083-eb85bb6f913e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/372548de-05b7-4bb1-8083-eb85bb6f913e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Commit 1261ab1b2b (merge PR #8 \"thread_safety_fix\") makes the global intern pool internally thread-safe via a pthread_mutex_t (behind SLOP_INTERN_THREADSAFE, now always defined in rust/build.rs) — see \"Mutex-protected intern pool under SLOP_INTERN_THREADSAFE\". rust/README.md's Thread Safety section is rewritten: it no longer says the intern pool \"is not thread-safe,\" and it drops the documented C_LOCK external-Mutex workaround entirely, so the previous constraint's rationale (\"multi-threaded callers ... must serialize access with a Mutex\") no longer holds. However the same README section states the Arena type \"is still !Send + !Sync — individual arenas must not be shared across threads. Each thread should create its own arena,\" so the top-line constraint survives for a narrower reason: per-arena allocation state, not the (now-synchronized) intern pool." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/372548de-05b7-4bb1-8083-eb85bb6f913e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "proposed" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/372548de-05b7-4bb1-8083-eb85bb6f913e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-09T07:10:05Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/372548de-05b7-4bb1-8083-eb85bb6f913e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Rust Arena must stay !Send + !Sync" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/3ccdc590-1b14-4250-a9eb-8fa0538e9ec3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/3ccdc590-1b14-4250-a9eb-8fa0538e9ec3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Refresh README verification proof counts" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/3ccdc590-1b14-4250-a9eb-8fa0538e9ec3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/3ccdc590-1b14-4250-a9eb-8fa0538e9ec3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Keeps the README's enumerated verification claims accurate as Z3-verified contract coverage grows, continuing the discipline the original decision established (exact counts, not unqualified \"formally verified\" claims) — the prior 55/8/3 counts and function lists are stale after PR #11's contract-strengthening commit and are replaced with the current 56/12/4 counts, which also document scm-eqp-mutual's completeness contract and a transitive-closure novelty contract for the first time." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/3ccdc590-1b14-4250-a9eb-8fa0538e9ec3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/3ccdc590-1b14-4250-a9eb-8fa0538e9ec3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-11T07:48:40Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/3ccdc590-1b14-4250-a9eb-8fa0538e9ec3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Refresh README verification proof counts" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/42d5b4e9-ba97-43e8-a41f-57c54e7328cf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/42d5b4e9-ba97-43e8-a41f-57c54e7328cf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Default CLI/release/test builds now define SLOP_ARENA_NO_CAP" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/42d5b4e9-ba97-43e8-a41f-57c54e7328cf> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/42d5b4e9-ba97-43e8-a41f-57c54e7328cf> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Commit d26d5120 (merge PR #3, \"Completing\") wires SLOP_ARENA_NO_CAP into the Makefile's default and release CFLAGS and into cli/slop.toml's and cli/tests/slop.toml's `no_arena_cap = true` build option, retiring the previous configurable ARENA=8589934592 (8GB) ceiling on those targets — so the earlier consequence (\"no build target does so, so default cap-enforcing behavior is unchanged\") no longer holds." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/42d5b4e9-ba97-43e8-a41f-57c54e7328cf> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/42d5b4e9-ba97-43e8-a41f-57c54e7328cf> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-08T00:55:37Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/42d5b4e9-ba97-43e8-a41f-57c54e7328cf> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Default CLI/release/test builds now define SLOP_ARENA_NO_CAP" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/4664a23f-a3f7-4ac1-a865-b23b7e5958d9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/4664a23f-a3f7-4ac1-a865-b23b7e5958d9> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "later-decision" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/4664a23f-a3f7-4ac1-a865-b23b7e5958d9> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Semantic sub-worker partitioning for parallel rule dispatch" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/4664a23f-a3f7-4ac1-a865-b23b7e5958d9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/4664a23f-a3f7-4ac1-a865-b23b7e5958d9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Commit 10f2845884 (\"adding more tests\") retires the one-thread-per-rule-group scheme: src/engine.slop's module doc changes from \"Each of the 5 rule groups (scm, cax, prp, eq, cls) runs in its own thread with its own arena\" to \"12 semantic sub-workers split across 5 rule groups (scm, cax, prp, eq, cls), each with its own thread and arena.\" spawn-rule-workers is rewritten from 5 closures (one per apply-*-rules call) to 12 closures, each calling a hand-picked subset of a rule group's individual rule functions (e.g. scm splits into scm-class/scm-prop/scm-domrng; cax splits into cax-infer/cax-check; prp splits into prp-char/prp-chain/prp-check; eq splits into eq-infer/eq-check; cls splits into cls-set/cls-ind) instead of calling the group's single apply-*-rules entry point. collect-worker-results' precondition changes from `(@pre {(list-len workers) == 5})` to `(@pre {(list-len workers) == 12})`." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/4664a23f-a3f7-4ac1-a865-b23b7e5958d9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/4664a23f-a3f7-4ac1-a865-b23b7e5958d9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-07T04:53:15Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/4664a23f-a3f7-4ac1-a865-b23b7e5958d9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Semantic sub-worker partitioning for parallel rule dispatch" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ab9b411c-1728-4d76-bc00-982407f0eb84> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ab9b411c-1728-4d76-bc00-982407f0eb84> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Semi-naive delta-based fixpoint evaluation (no redundant post-round filter)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ab9b411c-1728-4d76-bc00-982407f0eb84> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ab9b411c-1728-4d76-bc00-982407f0eb84> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "PR #2 (\"performance\", commit 10bc6356 merging ee866f6) removes the post-round \"filter out triples already in graph\" pass in engine.slop's engine-run-iteration (sequential path) and apply-all-rules-parallel's merge step (parallel path), because it was fully redundant: every individual rule already checks `(not (indexed-graph-contains g inferred))` before adding a triple to its own result list, and delta-add's `seen` hash set (see \"Use hash Set for O(1) Delta deduplication\") already deduplicates triples merged in from multiple rules. Evidence: src/engine.slop diff -- both branches drop their `(let ((mut filtered ...)) (for-each (t (. combined triples)) (when (not (indexed-graph-contains g t)) ...)) (ok filtered))` pattern in favor of returning `combined`/`result` directly, replaced by the comment \"Each rule already checks (indexed-graph-contains g inferred) before adding, and delta-add deduplicates across rules via (set-has seen t).\"" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ab9b411c-1728-4d76-bc00-982407f0eb84> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ab9b411c-1728-4d76-bc00-982407f0eb84> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-06T18:09:05Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ab9b411c-1728-4d76-bc00-982407f0eb84> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Semi-naive delta-based fixpoint evaluation (no redundant post-round filter)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/b1330b6d-5bbc-49fa-878a-1d190339714e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/b1330b6d-5bbc-49fa-878a-1d190339714e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "later-decision" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/b1330b6d-5bbc-49fa-878a-1d190339714e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Consume shared C modules via slop-std-sys/slop-rdf-sys" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/b1330b6d-5bbc-49fa-878a-1d190339714e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/b1330b6d-5bbc-49fa-878a-1d190339714e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "growl adopted slop-sys v0.2.1 (the slop-std-sys and slop-rdf-sys crates) as external providers of the shared modules (common, file, index, list, rdf, serialize_ttl, strlib, thread, ttl, vocab, xsd) that were previously vendored wholesale into rust/csrc/ by the `crate-vendor` Makefile target. Vendoring those modules a second time would make a consumer that links both the growl crate and slop-std-sys/slop-rdf-sys directly collide on duplicate C symbols, so `crate-vendor` now filters them out and build.rs compiles only growl's own modules, linking against the two -sys crates' native archives for the rest." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/b1330b6d-5bbc-49fa-878a-1d190339714e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/b1330b6d-5bbc-49fa-878a-1d190339714e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-10T18:10:28Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/b1330b6d-5bbc-49fa-878a-1d190339714e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Consume shared C modules via slop-std-sys/slop-rdf-sys" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e6e3fb80-6b6d-4d93-8751-8835b8e1fbdc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e6e3fb80-6b6d-4d93-8751-8835b8e1fbdc> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Loop-invariant soundness proofs dropped for memory-heavy rule functions" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e6e3fb80-6b6d-4d93-8751-8835b8e1fbdc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e6e3fb80-6b6d-4d93-8751-8835b8e1fbdc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Commit 75b17fd (\"significant fixes for memory issues\") deletes the per-loop @loop-invariant soundness blocks the superseded constraint recorded for cax-sco, cax-eqc1, cax-eqc2 (src/rules/cax.slop) and cls-hv1 (src/rules/cls.slop): each function's for-each over an indexed-graph-match-materialized list is replaced by a callback passed to the new indexed-graph-for-each primitive (see \"Stream graph matches via indexed-graph-for-each\"), and the callback form has no site to restate a per-iteration @loop-invariant, so the annotations were removed rather than ported. This trades away Z3-verified soundness coverage for these four rules in exchange for no longer materializing full match-result lists in the arena, which was the source of the memory growth this commit fixes. The other functions the superseded constraint named — cls-hv2, prp-dom, prp-rng — are not touched by this commit's cax.slop/cls.slop hunks, so their loop-invariant coverage is presumed unchanged pending confirmation in a later episode." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e6e3fb80-6b6d-4d93-8751-8835b8e1fbdc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "proposed" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e6e3fb80-6b6d-4d93-8751-8835b8e1fbdc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-04T23:49:15Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/e6e3fb80-6b6d-4d93-8751-8835b8e1fbdc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Loop-invariant soundness proofs dropped for memory-heavy rule functions" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ed5a7337-22b1-4850-ba9b-b80951349d8e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ed5a7337-22b1-4850-ba9b-b80951349d8e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Fast mode runs most consistency checks" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ed5a7337-22b1-4850-ba9b-b80951349d8e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ed5a7337-22b1-4850-ba9b-b80951349d8e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The prior \"Opt-in fast reasoning mode (--fast)\" decision specified that --fast skips cax-dw, cax-adc, prp-asyp, prp-irp, prp-pdw, eq-diff1/2/3, cls-nothing2, cls-com, and cls-maxc1/2. This commit reverses that for the consistency-check subset (cax-dw, cax-adc, prp-asyp, prp-irp, prp-pdw, prp-adp, prp-npa1/2, cls-nothing2, cls-com), which now run unconditionally in fast mode, keeping only eq-diff1/2/3, eq-ref, and the cardinality rules skipped -- explicitly to match the inference coverage of the `reasonable` reference reasoner newly added to the benchmark comparison harness." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ed5a7337-22b1-4850-ba9b-b80951349d8e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ed5a7337-22b1-4850-ba9b-b80951349d8e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-09T06:09:50Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ed5a7337-22b1-4850-ba9b-b80951349d8e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Fast mode runs most consistency checks" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee0685a6-f624-4534-96ee-a648f3702cbc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee0685a6-f624-4534-96ee-a648f3702cbc> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Opt-in --complete mode plus partial dt-* validation" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee0685a6-f624-4534-96ee-a648f3702cbc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee0685a6-f624-4534-96ee-a648f3702cbc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Commit cd5cee9a68 (merge PR #4 \"dt_rules\") partially reverses the prior \"OWL 2 RL rule coverage completion\" decision, which left prp-ap, cls-thing, cls-nothing1, and all of dt-* (Table 8) deliberately unimplemented at 70/78 (90%). This commit implements prp-ap, cls-thing, and cls-nothing1 -- but gates them behind a new opt-in `--complete`/`-c` CLI flag rather than enabling them by default, because (per the new README \"Complete Mode\" section) \"these rules are spec-correct but produce triples with zero practical inference value\" and exist mainly \"for conformance testing against other reasoners like owlrl.\" Separately, it implements dt-type1 and dt-not-type unconditionally (minimal datatype validation), while dt-type2, dt-eq, and dt-diff remain unimplemented -- the README explicitly notes dt-eq/dt-diff are skipped because \"even owlrl skips\" them. Net effect: coverage moves from 70/78 (90%) to 75/78 (96%)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee0685a6-f624-4534-96ee-a648f3702cbc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee0685a6-f624-4534-96ee-a648f3702cbc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-08T06:51:50Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ee0685a6-f624-4534-96ee-a648f3702cbc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Opt-in --complete mode plus partial dt-* validation" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f43567a1-7dde-4c02-bd2e-44b74644b825> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Rationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f43567a1-7dde-4c02-bd2e-44b74644b825> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rationale: Parallel worker infrastructure wired into main loop" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f43567a1-7dde-4c02-bd2e-44b74644b825> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James Adam <jcadam@startmail.com>" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f43567a1-7dde-4c02-bd2e-44b74644b825> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Commit 95c5860 (PR #1, \"thread_it\") wires the previously-scaffolded fork-join infrastructure into the live dispatch path: apply-all-rules now calls apply-all-rules-parallel (which in turn calls spawn-rule-workers / collect-worker-results) whenever config.worker-count > 1 and the iteration is not 0, so the prior \"scaffolded but not wired in, single-threaded path only, deferred to a later commit\" state no longer holds — this is that later commit." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f43567a1-7dde-4c02-bd2e-44b74644b825> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f43567a1-7dde-4c02-bd2e-44b74644b825> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-02-06T04:49:33Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/f43567a1-7dde-4c02-bd2e-44b74644b825> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Rationale: Parallel worker infrastructure wired into main loop" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
